NIFT_TANSTACK_DOCUMENT_V1
{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The OpenAI adapter provides access to OpenAI's models, including GPT-4o, GPT-5, image generation (DALL-E), text-to-speech (TTS), and audio transcription (Whisper)."}]},{"type":"blockquote","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Using a third-party provider that speaks the OpenAI API (DeepSeek, Moonshot/Kimi, Together, Fireworks, a local LM Studio/vLLM server, …)? See the "},{"type":"link","href":"./openai-compatible","children":[{"type":"text","value":"OpenAI-Compatible Adapter"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for a generic "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"openaiCompatible({ baseURL, apiKey, models })"},{"type":"text","value":" factory."}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"installation","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Installation"}]},{"type":"component","name":"tabs","attributes":{"variant":"package-manager","mode":"install"},"children":[],"properties":{"data-package-manager-meta":"{\"packagesByFramework\":{\"react\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-openai\"]],\"vue\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-openai\"]],\"solid\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-openai\"]],\"svelte\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-openai\"]],\"preact\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-openai\"]],\"angular\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-openai\"]],\"vanilla\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-openai\"]],\"octane\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-openai\"]]},\"mode\":\"install\"}"}},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"basic-usage","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Basic Usage"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { chat } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiText } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: openaiText(\"gpt-5.2\"),\n  messages: [{ role: \"user\", content: \"Hello!\" }],\n});","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"chat-completions-api","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Chat Completions API"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai-openai"},{"type":"text","value":" ships two text adapters that hit different OpenAI endpoints. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"openaiText"},{"type":"text","value":" (default) calls the Responses API ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"/v1/responses"},{"type":"text","value":"). "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"openaiChatCompletions"},{"type":"text","value":" calls the older Chat Completions API ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"/v1/chat/completions"},{"type":"text","value":")."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pick whichever fits your wire format and feature needs:"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"openaiText"},{"type":"text","value":" (Responses)"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"openaiChatCompletions"},{"type":"text","value":" (Chat Completions)"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Endpoint"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"/v1/responses"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"/v1/chat/completions"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Reasoning summaries"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Yes — set "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"modelOptions.reasoning.summary: 'auto'"},{"type":"text","value":" to surface reasoning text via "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"REASONING_*"},{"type":"text","value":" events"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"No — reasoning tokens are still consumed but cannot be exposed"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Wire-format compatibility"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"OpenAI-only"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Matches the older de-facto industry shape (Grok, Groq, OpenRouter, many local model servers)"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Structured output streaming"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"text.format: { type: 'json_schema', strict: true }"},{"type":"text","value":" + "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"stream: true"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"response_format: { type: 'json_schema', strict: true }"},{"type":"text","value":" + "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"stream: true"}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"openaiText"},{"type":"text","value":" when you want reasoning-summary streaming or OpenAI-specific Responses features. Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"openaiChatCompletions"},{"type":"text","value":" when you're migrating off a Chat-Completions-style provider, share request-building code with other Chat-Completions adapters in your stack, or want the more battle-tested wire format."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { chat } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiChatCompletions } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: openaiChatCompletions(\"gpt-5.2\"),\n  messages: [{ role: \"user\", content: \"Hello!\" }],\n});","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"With an explicit API key:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { chat } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { createOpenaiChatCompletions } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\n\nconst adapter = createOpenaiChatCompletions(\"gpt-5.2\", process.env.OPENAI_API_KEY!, {\n  // organization, baseURL, headers — all optional\n});\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter,\n  messages: [{ role: \"user\", content: \"Hello!\" }],\n});","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Both adapters work identically with "},{"type":"link","href":"../structured-outputs/overview","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Structured Outputs"}]},{"type":"text","value":" — including "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"stream: true"},{"type":"text","value":" — and accept the same "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"modelOptions"},{"type":"text","value":" (temperature, top_p, max_tokens, stop, …). The reasoning section below applies to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"openaiText"},{"type":"text","value":"; "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"openaiChatCompletions"},{"type":"text","value":" accepts "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"modelOptions.reasoning.effort"},{"type":"text","value":" but cannot stream summary text."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"basic-usage-custom-api-key","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Basic Usage - Custom API Key"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { chat } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { createOpenaiChat } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\n\nconst adapter = createOpenaiChat(\"gpt-5.2\", process.env.OPENAI_API_KEY!, {\n  // ... your config options\n});\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter,\n  messages: [{ role: \"user\", content: \"Hello!\" }],\n});","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"sign-in-with-chatgpt-byok","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Sign in with ChatGPT (BYOK)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Many of your users have a ChatGPT plan but no API key. Let them sign in with ChatGPT. The token bills their ChatGPT plan, not your account."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The helpers in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai-openai/siwc"},{"type":"text","value":" put the access token into the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"openai"},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"link","href":"../advanced/byok","children":[{"type":"text","value":"BYOK"}]},{"type":"text","value":" slot. Your relay reads it like a pasted key."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Before you start, check these limits:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"OpenAI allows this sign-in only for open-source and locally hosted apps. For a hosted app, fill in the "},{"type":"link","href":"https://openai.com/form/sign-in-with-chatgpt-interest/","children":[{"type":"text","value":"interest form"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"OpenAI redirects only to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"127.0.0.1"},{"type":"text","value":". Something must answer on that address. Vite listens on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"::1"},{"type":"text","value":" by default. The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ts-react-chat"},{"type":"text","value":" example runs a small script on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"127.0.0.1:3000"},{"type":"text","value":" that redirects to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"localhost:3000"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Keep the app on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"localhost"},{"type":"text","value":", because passkey storage does not work on an IP address. The callback lands on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"127.0.0.1"},{"type":"text","value":", then "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"completeChatGptSignIn"},{"type":"text","value":" sends the browser back to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"localhost"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The callback page must be at "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"/auth/callback"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"1-add-the-sign-in-button","children":[{"type":"text","value":"1. Add the sign-in button"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Call "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"startChatGptSignIn"},{"type":"text","value":" from a click. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"agentName"},{"type":"text","value":" is your app name. OpenAI shows it on the consent screen."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { startChatGptSignIn } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai/siwc\";\n\nexport function ChatGptButton() {\n  return (\n    <button\n      type=\"button\"\n      onClick={() => {\n        void startChatGptSignIn({ agentName: \"My App\" });\n      }}\n    >\n      Continue with ChatGPT\n    </button>\n  );\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"2-finish-on-auth-callback","children":[{"type":"text","value":"2. Finish on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"/auth/callback"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Render this component on the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"/auth/callback"},{"type":"text","value":" route. It exchanges the code when the page loads. Then the user clicks to save."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { useEffect, useRef, useState } from \"react\";\nimport {\n  completeChatGptSignIn,\n  saveChatGptSignIn,\n} from \"@tanstack/ai-openai/siwc\";\nimport type { ChatGptSignIn } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai/siwc\";\nimport { byok } from \"./byok\";\n\nexport function ChatGptCallback() {\n  const started = useRef(false);\n  const [signIn, setSignIn] = useState<ChatGptSignIn | null>(null);\n  const [error, setError] = useState(\"\");\n\n  useEffect(() => {\n    // The code works one time. Strict Mode runs effects two times.\n    if (started.current) return;\n    started.current = true;\n    completeChatGptSignIn().then(setSignIn, (caught: unknown) => {\n      setError(caught instanceof Error ? caught.message : \"Sign-in failed\");\n    });\n  }, []);\n\n  if (error) return <p>{error}</p>;\n  if (!signIn) return <p>Finishing sign-in...</p>;\n  return (\n    <button\n      type=\"button\"\n      onClick={() => {\n        void saveChatGptSignIn(byok, signIn);\n      }}\n    >\n      Save ChatGPT sign-in\n    </button>\n  );\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The save needs a click because passkey storage shows a browser prompt. The refresh token goes into a second keyring slot. No send attaches that slot, so the refresh token stays in the browser."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"3-refresh-the-token","children":[{"type":"text","value":"3. Refresh the token"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The access token lasts one hour. Call "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"refreshChatGptSignIn"},{"type":"text","value":" on a timer:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { useEffect } from \"react\";\nimport { refreshChatGptSignIn } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai/siwc\";\nimport { byok } from \"./byok\";\n\nexport function useChatGptRefresh() {\n  useEffect(() => {\n    const refresh = () => {\n      refreshChatGptSignIn(byok).catch(console.error);\n    };\n    refresh();\n    const timer = setInterval(refresh, 60_000);\n    return () => clearInterval(timer);\n  }, []);\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The call does nothing until the token has less than five minutes left. If OpenAI rejects the refresh token, the call clears the sign-in. Then the user must sign in again."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"4-read-the-token-on-the-relay","children":[{"type":"text","value":"4. Read the token on the relay"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The relay code is the same as for a pasted key. Add "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"store: false"},{"type":"text","value":", because the ChatGPT route requires it."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import {\n  chat,\n  chatParamsFromRequest,\n  toServerSentEventsResponse,\n} from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { createOpenaiChat } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\nimport { openaiByok } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai/byok\";\nimport { byokMissing, getByokKey } from \"@tanstack/ai/byok/server\";\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const params = await chatParamsFromRequest(request);\n  const apiKey = getByokKey(request, openaiByok);\n  if (!apiKey) return byokMissing(openaiByok);\n\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: createOpenaiChat(\"gpt-6-astra\", apiKey),\n    messages: params.messages,\n    threadId: params.threadId,\n    runId: params.runId,\n    modelOptions: { store: false },\n  });\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream);\n}","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"store: false"},{"type":"text","value":" also works with an API key. A ChatGPT token does not start with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sk-"},{"type":"text","value":", so use that test if you must send different options."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The ChatGPT route has these limits:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use a model that the user's ChatGPT plan includes."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Do not send "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"temperature"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"top_p"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"max_output_tokens"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"metadata"},{"type":"text","value":", or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"previous_response_id"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Hosted tools do not work. This includes image generation, file search, code interpreter, computer use, and hosted MCP."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Audio input and transcription do not work."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Click "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Continue with ChatGPT"}]},{"type":"text","value":", approve, save, then send a message. The relay calls OpenAI on the user's ChatGPT plan."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ts-react-chat"},{"type":"text","value":" example has this flow in its key dialog."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"configuration","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Configuration"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { createOpenaiChat, type OpenAITextConfig } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\n\nconst config: Omit<OpenAITextConfig, \"apiKey\"> = {\n  organization: \"org-...\", // Optional\n  baseURL: \"https://api.openai.com/v1\", // Optional, for custom endpoints\n};\n\nconst adapter = createOpenaiChat(\"gpt-5.2\", process.env.OPENAI_API_KEY!, config);","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"tools-that-cannot-use-strict-mode","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Tools that cannot use strict mode"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"OpenAI holds tool arguments to the schema only when the tool is sent with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"strict: true"},{"type":"text","value":". Some schemas cannot be strict, for example a schema that uses "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"$ref"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"z.any()"},{"type":"text","value":", or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"z.record()"},{"type":"text","value":". The adapter sends these tools with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"strict: false"},{"type":"text","value":", so the tool still works. The model can then return arguments that do not match the schema."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"In development, the adapter logs a warning once for each of these tools:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"tool \"lookup_user\" sent with strict: false: schema uses $ref, which strict mode does not support","lang":"txt"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"To get strict mode back, change the schema so that the reason goes away. If you accept a non-strict tool, turn the warning off in the adapter config:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { createOpenaiChat } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\n\nconst adapter = createOpenaiChat(\"gpt-6-astra\", process.env.OPENAI_API_KEY!, {\n  strictFallbackWarning: false,\n});","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The warning never runs when "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"NODE_ENV"},{"type":"text","value":" is "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"production"},{"type":"text","value":". The same option works on every adapter built on the OpenAI API, for example Groq, Bedrock, and Vercel AI Gateway."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"example-chat-completion","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example: Chat Completion"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { chat, toServerSentEventsResponse } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiText } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const { messages } = await request.json();\n\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: openaiText(\"gpt-5.2\"),\n    messages,\n  });\n\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream);\n}","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"example-with-tools","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example: With Tools"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { chat, toServerSentEventsResponse, toolDefinition } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiText } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\nimport { z } from \"zod\";\n\nconst getWeatherDef = toolDefinition({\n  name: \"get_weather\",\n  description: \"Get the current weather\",\n  inputSchema: z.object({\n    location: z.string(),\n  }),\n});\n\nconst getWeather = getWeatherDef.server(async ({ location }) => {\n  // Fetch weather data\n  return { temperature: 72, conditions: \"sunny\" };\n});\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const { messages } = await request.json();\n\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: openaiText(\"gpt-5.2\"),\n    messages,\n    tools: [getWeather],\n  });\n\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream);\n}","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"model-options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Model Options"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"OpenAI supports various provider-specific options. Sampling parameters live here too — "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"temperature"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"top_p"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"max_output_tokens"},{"type":"text","value":" (the Responses API token-limit key) — rather than as root-level props on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat()"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { chat } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiText } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: openaiText(\"gpt-5.2\"),\n  messages: [{ role: \"user\", content: \"Hello!\" }],\n  modelOptions: {\n    temperature: 0.7,\n    max_output_tokens: 1000,\n    top_p: 0.9,\n  },\n});","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"blockquote","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"openaiChatCompletions"},{"type":"text","value":" adapter targets "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"/v1/chat/completions"},{"type":"text","value":", where the token-limit key is "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"max_tokens"},{"type":"text","value":" (not "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"max_output_tokens"},{"type":"text","value":"). If you previously passed "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"temperature"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"topP"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"maxTokens"},{"type":"text","value":" at the root of "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat()"},{"type":"text","value":", see "},{"type":"link","href":"../migration/sampling-options-to-model-options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Moving Sampling Options into modelOptions"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"reasoning","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Reasoning"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Enable reasoning for models that support it (e.g., GPT-5, O3). This allows the model to show its reasoning process, which is streamed as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"thinking"},{"type":"text","value":" chunks:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"modelOptions: {\n  reasoning: {\n    effort: \"medium\", // \"none\" | \"minimal\" | \"low\" | \"medium\" | \"high\"\n    summary: \"detailed\", // \"auto\" | \"detailed\" (optional)\n  },\n}","lang":"typescript","meta":"ignore"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When reasoning is enabled, the model's reasoning process is streamed separately from the response text and appears as a collapsible thinking section in the UI."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"summarization","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Summarization"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Summarize long text content:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { summarize } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiSummarize } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\n\nconst result = await summarize({\n  adapter: openaiSummarize(\"gpt-5-mini\"),\n  text: \"Your long text to summarize...\",\n  maxLength: 100,\n  style: \"concise\", // \"concise\" | \"bullet-points\" | \"paragraph\"\n});\n\nconsole.log(result.summary);","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"embeddings","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Embeddings"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Generate embedding vectors with the text-embedding-3 models:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { embed } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiEmbedding } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\n\nconst result = await embed({\n  adapter: openaiEmbedding(\"text-embedding-3-small\"),\n  input: [\"a red guitar\", \"a blue drum kit\"],\n});\n\nconsole.log(result.embeddings[0]?.vector);\nconsole.log(result.usage?.promptTokens);","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Both models support Matryoshka dimension reduction via the top-level "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"dimensions"},{"type":"text","value":" option:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { embed } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiEmbedding } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\n\nconst result = await embed({\n  adapter: openaiEmbedding(\"text-embedding-3-large\"),\n  input: \"a red guitar\",\n  dimensions: 1024,\n});","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"See the "},{"type":"link","href":"../embeddings.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Embeddings guide"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for the full API."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"image-generation","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Image Generation"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Generate images:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { generateImage } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiImage } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\n\nconst result = await generateImage({\n  adapter: openaiImage(\"gpt-image-2\"),\n  prompt: \"A futuristic cityscape at sunset\",\n  numberOfImages: 1,\n  size: \"1024x1024\",\n});\n\nconsole.log(result.images);","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"image-model-options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Image Model Options"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { generateImage } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiImage } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\n\nconst result = await generateImage({\n  adapter: openaiImage(\"gpt-image-2\"),\n  prompt: \"...\",\n  modelOptions: {\n    quality: \"high\", // \"high\" | \"medium\" | \"low\" | \"auto\"\n  },\n});","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"text-to-speech","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Text-to-Speech"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Generate speech from text:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { generateSpeech } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiSpeech } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\n\nconst result = await generateSpeech({\n  adapter: openaiSpeech(\"tts-1\"),\n  text: \"Hello, welcome to TanStack AI!\",\n  voice: \"alloy\",\n  format: \"mp3\",\n});\n\n// result.audio contains base64-encoded audio\nconsole.log(result.format); // \"mp3\"","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"tts-voices","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TTS Voices"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Available voices: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"alloy"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"echo"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fable"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onyx"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"nova"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"shimmer"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ash"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ballad"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"coral"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sage"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"verse"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"tts-model-options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TTS Model Options"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { generateSpeech } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiSpeech } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\n\nconst result = await generateSpeech({\n  adapter: openaiSpeech(\"tts-1-hd\"),\n  text: \"High quality speech\",\n  modelOptions: {\n    instructions: \"Speak slowly and clearly.\", // voice instructions (not supported by tts-1/tts-1-hd)\n  },\n});","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"transcription","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Transcription"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Transcribe audio to text:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { generateTranscription } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiTranscription } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\nimport { audioFile } from \"./audio\";\n\nconst result = await generateTranscription({\n  adapter: openaiTranscription(\"whisper-1\"),\n  audio: audioFile, // File object or base64 string\n  language: \"en\",\n});\n\nconsole.log(result.text); // Transcribed text","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"transcription-model-options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Transcription Model Options"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { generateTranscription } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiTranscription } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\nimport { audioFile } from \"./audio\";\n\nconst result = await generateTranscription({\n  adapter: openaiTranscription(\"whisper-1\"),\n  audio: audioFile,\n  responseFormat: \"verbose_json\",\n  prompt: \"Technical terms: API, SDK\",\n  modelOptions: {\n    temperature: 0,\n    timestamp_granularities: [\"word\", \"segment\"],\n  },\n});\n\n// Access the transcribed text\nconsole.log(result.text);","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"speaker-diarization","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Speaker Diarization"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"gpt-4o-transcribe-diarize"},{"type":"text","value":" for speaker-labeled transcripts:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { generateTranscription } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiTranscription } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\nimport { meetingAudioFile } from \"./audio\";\n\nconst result = await generateTranscription({\n  adapter: openaiTranscription(\"gpt-4o-transcribe-diarize\"),\n  audio: meetingAudioFile,\n  modelOptions: {\n    known_speaker_names: [\"agent\", \"customer\"],\n    known_speaker_references: [\n      \"data:audio/wav;base64,...\",\n      \"data:audio/wav;base64,...\",\n    ],\n  },\n});\n\nfor (const segment of result.segments ?? []) {\n  console.log(segment.speaker, segment.start, segment.end, segment.text);\n}","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When no response format is specified, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"gpt-4o-transcribe-diarize"},{"type":"text","value":" requests default to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"response_format: \"diarized_json\""},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chunking_strategy: \"auto\""},{"type":"text","value":"; passing a top-level "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"responseFormat"},{"type":"text","value":" of "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"\"json\""},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"\"text\""},{"type":"text","value":" opts out of speaker segments. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"known_speaker_names"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"known_speaker_references"},{"type":"text","value":" must be provided together (up to 4, matching lengths). OpenAI does not support "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"prompt"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"include"},{"type":"text","value":", or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"timestamp_granularities"},{"type":"text","value":" with diarized transcription."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"evaluate","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Evaluate"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Sometimes you need an answer that your code can branch on, not chat text. Examples are a queue name, an urgency level, or a yes or no.\nUse "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"openaiDecider"},{"type":"text","value":" with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"decide()"},{"type":"text","value":" to ask typed questions about one shared "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"state"},{"type":"text","value":". The adapter calls the OpenAI Decisions API ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"/v1/decisions"},{"type":"text","value":"):"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { decide, choice, score, boolean } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiDecider } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\n\nconst ticket = {\n  subject: \"Charged twice for the same invoice\",\n  body: \"Please refund the extra payment.\",\n};\n\nconst result = await decide({\n  adapter: openaiDecider(\"gpt-6-luna\"),\n  state: ticket,\n  questions: {\n    queue: choice({\n      instructions: \"Which team should handle this ticket?\",\n      options: {\n        billing: \"Payments, invoices, refunds\",\n        tech: \"Bugs, outages, integrations\",\n        sales: \"Pricing, upgrades, new accounts\",\n      },\n    }),\n    urgency: score({\n      instructions: \"How urgent is this ticket?\",\n      levels: [\"low\", \"medium\", \"high\"],\n    }),\n    refund: boolean({\n      instructions: \"Is the customer asking for a refund?\",\n    }),\n  },\n});\n\nconsole.log(result.queue.value); // \"billing\"\nconsole.log(result.urgency.value); // \"medium\"\nconsole.log(result.refund.value); // true\nconsole.log(result.meta.usage);","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"openaiDecider"},{"type":"text","value":" reads "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"OPENAI_API_KEY"},{"type":"text","value":" from the environment. To pass a key yourself, use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createOpenaiDecider(\"gpt-6-luna\", \"sk-...\")"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Good to know:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"gpt-6-luna"},{"type":"text","value":" is the only Decisions model."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"An object "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"state"},{"type":"text","value":" goes to OpenAI as JSON text."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If OpenAI refuses to answer a question, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"decide()"},{"type":"text","value":" throws an error with the name of that question."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"boolean()"},{"type":"text","value":" criteria work. The adapter adds the true and false meanings to the instructions."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"See the "},{"type":"link","href":"../evaluate/evaluate","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Evaluate guide"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for question helpers, the result shape, abort, and middleware."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"environment-variables","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Environment Variables"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Set your API key in environment variables:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...","lang":"bash"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"api-reference","children":[{"type":"text","value":"API Reference"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Every factory pair follows the same shape: the short factory ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"openaiText"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"openaiImage"},{"type":"text","value":", …) reads "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"OPENAI_API_KEY"},{"type":"text","value":" from the environment, while the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"create*"},{"type":"text","value":" variant takes an explicit API key. Both take "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"model"},{"type":"text","value":" as the first argument."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"openaitext-model-config","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"openaiText(model, config?)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Creates an OpenAI text adapter against the Responses API ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"/v1/responses"},{"type":"text","value":") using "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"OPENAI_API_KEY"},{"type":"text","value":" from the environment."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Parameters:"}]}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"model"},{"type":"text","value":" - OpenAI chat model id (e.g. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"\"gpt-5.2\""},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"\"gpt-4o-mini\""},{"type":"text","value":")"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"config?.organization"},{"type":"text","value":" - Organization ID (optional)"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"config?.baseURL"},{"type":"text","value":" - Custom base URL (optional)"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"createopenaichat-model-apikey-config","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createOpenaiChat(model, apiKey, config?)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Creates an OpenAI text adapter (Responses API) with an explicit API key."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"openaichatcompletions-model-config","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"openaiChatCompletions(model, config?)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Creates an OpenAI text adapter that targets "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"/v1/chat/completions"},{"type":"text","value":" instead of the Responses API. See "},{"type":"link","href":"#chat-completions-api","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Chat Completions API"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for when to use this over "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"openaiText"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"createopenaichatcompletions-model-apikey-config","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createOpenaiChatCompletions(model, apiKey, config?)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Creates an OpenAI chat-completions adapter with an explicit API key."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"openaisummarize-model-config-createopenaisummarize-model-apikey-config","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"openaiSummarize(model, config?)"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createOpenaiSummarize(model, apiKey, config?)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Creates an OpenAI summarization adapter."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"openaiimage-model-config-createopenaiimage-model-apikey-config","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"openaiImage(model, config?)"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createOpenaiImage(model, apiKey, config?)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Creates an OpenAI image generation adapter (DALL-E, gpt-image)."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"openaispeech-model-config-createopenaispeech-model-apikey-config","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"openaiSpeech(model, config?)"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createOpenaiSpeech(model, apiKey, config?)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Creates an OpenAI text-to-speech adapter."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"openaitranscription-model-config-createopenaitranscription-model-apikey-config","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"openaiTranscription(model, config?)"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createOpenaiTranscription(model, apiKey, config?)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Creates an OpenAI transcription adapter for Whisper, GPT-4o transcription, and GPT-4o diarized transcription models."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"openaivideo-model-config-createopenaivideo-model-apikey-config","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"openaiVideo(model, config?)"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createOpenaiVideo(model, apiKey, config?)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Creates an OpenAI video generation adapter (Sora). "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Experimental."}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"openaidecider-model-config-createopenaidecider-model-apikey-config","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"openaiDecider(model, config?)"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createOpenaiDecider(model, apiKey, config?)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Creates an OpenAI evaluate adapter for "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"decide()"},{"type":"text","value":". See "},{"type":"link","href":"#evaluate","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Evaluate"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for usage."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"openairealtime-openairealtimetoken","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"openaiRealtime(...)"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"openaiRealtimeToken(...)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Realtime voice adapters. See "},{"type":"link","href":"../media/realtime-chat","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Realtime Voice Chat"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for usage."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"next-steps","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Next Steps"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../getting-started/quick-start","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Getting Started"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Learn the basics"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../tools/tools","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Tools Guide"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Learn about tools"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./anthropic","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Other Adapters"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Explore other providers"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"provider-tools","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Provider Tools"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"OpenAI exposes several native tools beyond user-defined function calls.\nImport them from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai-openai/tools"},{"type":"text","value":" and pass them into\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat({ tools: [...] })"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"blockquote","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For the full concept, a comparison matrix, and type-gating details, see\n"},{"type":"link","href":"../tools/provider-tools.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Provider Tools"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"websearchtool","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"webSearchTool"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Enables the model to run a web search and return grounded results with\ncitations. Pass a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"WebSearchToolConfig"},{"type":"text","value":" object (typed from the OpenAI SDK)\nto configure the tool."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { chat } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiText } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\nimport { webSearchTool } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai/tools\";\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: openaiText(\"gpt-5.2\"),\n  messages: [{ role: \"user\", content: \"What's new in AI this week?\" }],\n  tools: [webSearchTool({ type: \"web_search\" })],\n});","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Supported models:"}]},{"type":"text","value":" GPT-4o, GPT-5, and Responses API-capable models. See "},{"type":"link","href":"../tools/provider-tools.md#which-models-support-which-tools","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Provider Tools"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"websearchpreviewtool","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"webSearchPreviewTool"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The preview variant of web search with additional options for controlling\nsearch context size and user location. Use this when you want fine-grained\ncontrol over the search context sent to the model."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { chat } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiText } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\nimport { webSearchPreviewTool } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai/tools\";\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: openaiText(\"gpt-5.2\"),\n  messages: [{ role: \"user\", content: \"Latest news about TypeScript\" }],\n  tools: [\n    webSearchPreviewTool({\n      type: \"web_search_preview_2025_03_11\",\n      search_context_size: \"high\",\n    }),\n  ],\n});","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Supported models:"}]},{"type":"text","value":" GPT-4o and above. See "},{"type":"link","href":"../tools/provider-tools.md#which-models-support-which-tools","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Provider Tools"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When the model uses hosted web search, the assistant tool-call part includes\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"metadata.providerExecuted: true"},{"type":"text","value":" and the normalized "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"metadata.sources"},{"type":"text","value":" array.\nOpenAI's raw search call and URL citations stay under "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"metadata.openai"},{"type":"text","value":". The\nagent loop does not execute this call in your application, and the adapter\nreplays the raw response items on the next turn."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"filesearchtool","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fileSearchTool"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Searches OpenAI vector stores that you have pre-populated, letting the model\nretrieve relevant document chunks. Provide the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"vector_store_ids"},{"type":"text","value":" to search\nand optionally limit results with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"max_num_results"},{"type":"text","value":" (1–50)."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { chat } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiText } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\nimport { fileSearchTool } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai/tools\";\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: openaiText(\"gpt-5.2\"),\n  messages: [{ role: \"user\", content: \"What does the handbook say about PTO?\" }],\n  tools: [\n    fileSearchTool({\n      type: \"file_search\",\n      vector_store_ids: [\"vs_abc123\"],\n      max_num_results: 5,\n    }),\n  ],\n});","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Supported models:"}]},{"type":"text","value":" GPT-4o and above. See "},{"type":"link","href":"../tools/provider-tools.md#which-models-support-which-tools","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Provider Tools"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"imagegenerationtool","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"imageGenerationTool"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Allows the model to generate images inline during a conversation using\nDALL-E/GPT-Image. Pass quality, size, and style options via the config object."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { chat } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiText } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\nimport { imageGenerationTool } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai/tools\";\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: openaiText(\"gpt-5.2\"),\n  messages: [{ role: \"user\", content: \"Draw a logo for my app\" }],\n  tools: [\n    imageGenerationTool({\n      quality: \"high\",\n      size: \"1024x1024\",\n    }),\n  ],\n});","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Supported models:"}]},{"type":"text","value":" GPT-5 and GPT-Image-capable models. See "},{"type":"link","href":"../tools/provider-tools.md#which-models-support-which-tools","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Provider Tools"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"codeinterpretertool","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"codeInterpreterTool"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Gives the model a sandboxed Python execution environment. The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"container"},{"type":"text","value":"\nfield configures the execution environment; pass the full\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"CodeInterpreterToolConfig"},{"type":"text","value":" object."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { chat } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiText } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\nimport { codeInterpreterTool } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai/tools\";\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: openaiText(\"gpt-5.2\"),\n  messages: [{ role: \"user\", content: \"Analyse this CSV and plot a chart\" }],\n  tools: [\n    codeInterpreterTool({ type: \"code_interpreter\", container: { type: \"auto\" } }),\n  ],\n});","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Supported models:"}]},{"type":"text","value":" GPT-4o and above. See "},{"type":"link","href":"../tools/provider-tools.md#which-models-support-which-tools","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Provider Tools"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"mcptool","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"mcpTool"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Connects the model to a remote MCP (Model Context Protocol) server, exposing\nall its capabilities as callable tools. Provide either "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"server_url"},{"type":"text","value":" or\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"connector_id"},{"type":"text","value":" — not both."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { chat } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiText } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\nimport { mcpTool } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai/tools\";\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: openaiText(\"gpt-5.2\"),\n  messages: [{ role: \"user\", content: \"List my GitHub issues\" }],\n  tools: [\n    mcpTool({\n      server_url: \"https://mcp.example.com\",\n      server_label: \"github\",\n    }),\n  ],\n});","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Supported models:"}]},{"type":"text","value":" GPT-4o and above. See "},{"type":"link","href":"../tools/provider-tools.md#which-models-support-which-tools","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Provider Tools"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"computerusetool","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"computerUseTool"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Lets the model observe a virtual desktop via screenshots and interact with\nit using keyboard and mouse events. Provide the display dimensions and the\nexecution environment type."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { chat } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiText } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\nimport { computerUseTool } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai/tools\";\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: openaiText(\"computer-use-preview\"),\n  messages: [{ role: \"user\", content: \"Open Chrome and navigate to example.com\" }],\n  tools: [\n    computerUseTool({\n      type: \"computer_use_preview\",\n      display_width: 1024,\n      display_height: 768,\n      environment: \"browser\",\n    }),\n  ],\n});","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Supported models:"}]},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"computer-use-preview"},{"type":"text","value":". See "},{"type":"link","href":"../tools/provider-tools.md#which-models-support-which-tools","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Provider Tools"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"localshelltool","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"localShellTool"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The model returns a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"local_shell"},{"type":"text","value":" tool call. Your app runs the command. Then your app sends the output back on the next request. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"localShellTool()"},{"type":"text","value":" takes no arguments. Add it to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tools"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Match "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"toolName"},{"type":"text","value":" on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TOOL_CALL_START"},{"type":"text","value":". Read "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"input"},{"type":"text","value":" on the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TOOL_CALL_END"},{"type":"text","value":" with the same "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"toolCallId"},{"type":"text","value":". "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"input.command"},{"type":"text","value":" is the command. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"input.env"},{"type":"text","value":" is the environment variables."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { chat } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiText } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\nimport { localShellTool } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai/tools\";\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: openaiText(\"gpt-5.6\"),\n  messages: [{ role: \"user\", content: \"Run the test suite and summarise failures\" }],\n  tools: [localShellTool()],\n});\n\nlet localShellCallId: string | undefined;\nfor await (const chunk of stream) {\n  if (chunk.type === \"TOOL_CALL_START\" && chunk.toolName === \"local_shell\") {\n    localShellCallId = chunk.toolCallId;\n  }\n  if (chunk.type === \"TOOL_CALL_END\" && chunk.toolCallId === localShellCallId) {\n    console.log(chunk.input);\n  }\n}","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Send the command output as the tool result. Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ output: string }"},{"type":"text","value":", or a string. The next request sends "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"local_shell_call_output"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Supported models:"}]},{"type":"text","value":" GPT-5.x and other agent-capable models. See "},{"type":"link","href":"../tools/provider-tools.md#which-models-support-which-tools","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Provider Tools"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"shelltool","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"shellTool"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"shellTool()"},{"type":"text","value":" gives the model a shell. A container environment runs on OpenAI. A local environment runs in your app."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When your app must run the commands, pass "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"environment: { type: \"local\" }"},{"type":"text","value":". Match "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"toolName"},{"type":"text","value":" on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TOOL_CALL_START"},{"type":"text","value":". Read "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"input"},{"type":"text","value":" on the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TOOL_CALL_END"},{"type":"text","value":" with the same "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"toolCallId"},{"type":"text","value":". "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"input.commands"},{"type":"text","value":" is the command list. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"input.timeout_ms"},{"type":"text","value":" is the time limit. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"input.max_output_length"},{"type":"text","value":" is the output limit."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { chat } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiText } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\nimport { shellTool } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai/tools\";\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: openaiText(\"gpt-5.6\"),\n  messages: [{ role: \"user\", content: \"Count lines in all JS files\" }],\n  tools: [shellTool({ environment: { type: \"local\" } })],\n});\n\nlet shellCallId: string | undefined;\nfor await (const chunk of stream) {\n  if (chunk.type === \"TOOL_CALL_START\" && chunk.toolName === \"shell\") {\n    shellCallId = chunk.toolCallId;\n  }\n  if (chunk.type === \"TOOL_CALL_END\" && chunk.toolCallId === shellCallId) {\n    console.log(chunk.input);\n  }\n}","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Return one result per command:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const shellResult = {\n  output: [\n    {\n      stdout: \"12\\n\",\n      stderr: \"\",\n      outcome: { type: \"exit\" as const, exit_code: 0 },\n    },\n  ],\n};","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"outcome.type"},{"type":"text","value":" is "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"\"exit\""},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"\"timeout\""},{"type":"text","value":". The next request sends "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"shell_call_output"},{"type":"text","value":". If the same response has no "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"shell_call_output"},{"type":"text","value":", a shell call with no environment comes back to your app."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A container environment does not come back as a tool call. Pass "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"environment"},{"type":"text","value":" to attach that container and hosted skills."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Supported models:"}]},{"type":"text","value":" GPT-5.x and other agent-capable models. Responses API\nonly — Chat Completions does not support the shell tool. See "},{"type":"link","href":"../tools/provider-tools.md#which-models-support-which-tools","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Provider Tools"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"attaching-hosted-skills","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Attaching hosted skills"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pass "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"environment.skills"},{"type":"text","value":" to load provider-managed skill bundles into the\nshell's container (Responses API only)."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { chat, toServerSentEventsResponse } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiText } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\nimport { shellTool } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai/tools\";\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const { messages } = await request.json();\n\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: openaiText(\"gpt-5.2\"),\n    messages,\n    tools: [\n      shellTool({\n        environment: {\n          type: \"container_auto\",\n          skills: [\n            { type: \"skill_reference\", skill_id: \"skill_abc\", version: \"2\" },\n          ],\n        },\n      }),\n    ],\n  });\n\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream);\n}","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For the full reference — skill shape, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"version"},{"type":"text","value":" string format, and the\nAnthropic equivalent — see "},{"type":"link","href":"../tools/provider-skills.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Provider Skills"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"applypatchtool","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"applyPatchTool"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The model returns an "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"apply_patch"},{"type":"text","value":" tool call. Your app applies the diff. Then your app sends the result back. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"applyPatchTool()"},{"type":"text","value":" takes no arguments. Add it to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tools"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Match "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"toolName"},{"type":"text","value":" on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TOOL_CALL_START"},{"type":"text","value":". Read "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"input"},{"type":"text","value":" on the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TOOL_CALL_END"},{"type":"text","value":" with the same "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"toolCallId"},{"type":"text","value":". "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"input.operation"},{"type":"text","value":" is one file change. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"operation.type"},{"type":"text","value":" is "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"create_file"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"update_file"},{"type":"text","value":", or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"delete_file"},{"type":"text","value":". "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"operation.path"},{"type":"text","value":" is the file path. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"create_file"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"update_file"},{"type":"text","value":" also include "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"operation.diff"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { chat } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiText } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\nimport { applyPatchTool } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai/tools\";\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: openaiText(\"gpt-5.6\"),\n  messages: [{ role: \"user\", content: \"Fix the import paths in src/index.ts\" }],\n  tools: [applyPatchTool()],\n});\n\nlet patchCallId: string | undefined;\nfor await (const chunk of stream) {\n  if (chunk.type === \"TOOL_CALL_START\" && chunk.toolName === \"apply_patch\") {\n    patchCallId = chunk.toolCallId;\n  }\n  if (chunk.type === \"TOOL_CALL_END\" && chunk.toolCallId === patchCallId) {\n    console.log(chunk.input);\n  }\n}","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Send this object as the tool result. The next request sends "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"apply_patch_call_output"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"code","value":"const patchResult = {\n  status: \"completed\" as const,\n  output: \"Updated src/index.ts\",\n};","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If the patch fails, set "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"status"},{"type":"text","value":" to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"\"failed\""},{"type":"text","value":". Put the error text in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"output"},{"type":"text","value":". Keep "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"applyPatchTool()"},{"type":"text","value":" in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tools"},{"type":"text","value":" on the next request. A patch-only turn has no text. If you use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat({ stream: false })"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"text"},{"type":"text","value":" is empty. Read the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"apply_patch"},{"type":"text","value":" tool call from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chunks"},{"type":"text","value":" with the same checks as the loop above."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Supported models:"}]},{"type":"text","value":" GPT-5.x and other agent-capable models. See "},{"type":"link","href":"../tools/provider-tools.md#which-models-support-which-tools","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Provider Tools"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"customtool","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"customTool"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defines a custom Responses API tool with an explicit name, description, and\nformat. Use this when none of the structured tool types fits your use case.\nUnlike branded provider tools, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"customTool"},{"type":"text","value":" returns a plain "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Tool"},{"type":"text","value":" and is\naccepted by any chat model."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { chat } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiText } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\nimport { customTool } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai/tools\";\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: openaiText(\"gpt-5.2\"),\n  messages: [{ role: \"user\", content: \"Look up order #1234\" }],\n  tools: [\n    customTool({\n      type: \"custom\",\n      name: \"lookup_order\",\n      description: \"Look up the status of a customer order by order ID\",\n    }),\n  ],\n});","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Supported models:"}]},{"type":"text","value":" all Responses API models. See "},{"type":"link","href":"../tools/provider-tools.md#which-models-support-which-tools","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Provider Tools"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"installation","text":"Installation","level":2},{"id":"basic-usage","text":"Basic Usage","level":2},{"id":"chat-completions-api","text":"Chat Completions API","level":2},{"id":"basic-usage-custom-api-key","text":"Basic Usage - Custom API Key","level":2},{"id":"sign-in-with-chatgpt-byok","text":"Sign in with ChatGPT (BYOK)","level":2},{"id":"1-add-the-sign-in-button","text":"1. Add the sign-in button","level":3},{"id":"2-finish-on-auth-callback","text":"2. Finish on /auth/callback","level":3},{"id":"3-refresh-the-token","text":"3. Refresh the token","level":3},{"id":"4-read-the-token-on-the-relay","text":"4. Read the token on the relay","level":3},{"id":"configuration","text":"Configuration","level":2},{"id":"tools-that-cannot-use-strict-mode","text":"Tools that cannot use strict mode","level":3},{"id":"example-chat-completion","text":"Example: Chat Completion","level":2},{"id":"example-with-tools","text":"Example: With Tools","level":2},{"id":"model-options","text":"Model Options","level":2},{"id":"reasoning","text":"Reasoning","level":3},{"id":"summarization","text":"Summarization","level":2},{"id":"embeddings","text":"Embeddings","level":2},{"id":"image-generation","text":"Image Generation","level":2},{"id":"image-model-options","text":"Image Model Options","level":3},{"id":"text-to-speech","text":"Text-to-Speech","level":2},{"id":"tts-voices","text":"TTS Voices","level":3},{"id":"tts-model-options","text":"TTS Model Options","level":3},{"id":"transcription","text":"Transcription","level":2},{"id":"transcription-model-options","text":"Transcription Model Options","level":3},{"id":"speaker-diarization","text":"Speaker Diarization","level":3},{"id":"evaluate","text":"Evaluate","level":2},{"id":"environment-variables","text":"Environment Variables","level":2},{"id":"api-reference","text":"API Reference","level":2},{"id":"openaitext-model-config","text":"openaiText(model, config?)","level":3},{"id":"createopenaichat-model-apikey-config","text":"createOpenaiChat(model, apiKey, config?)","level":3},{"id":"openaichatcompletions-model-config","text":"openaiChatCompletions(model, config?)","level":3},{"id":"createopenaichatcompletions-model-apikey-config","text":"createOpenaiChatCompletions(model, apiKey, config?)","level":3},{"id":"openaisummarize-model-config-createopenaisummarize-model-apikey-config","text":"openaiSummarize(model, config?) / createOpenaiSummarize(model, apiKey, config?)","level":3},{"id":"openaiimage-model-config-createopenaiimage-model-apikey-config","text":"openaiImage(model, config?) / createOpenaiImage(model, apiKey, config?)","level":3},{"id":"openaispeech-model-config-createopenaispeech-model-apikey-config","text":"openaiSpeech(model, config?) / createOpenaiSpeech(model, apiKey, config?)","level":3},{"id":"openaitranscription-model-config-createopenaitranscription-model-apikey-config","text":"openaiTranscription(model, config?) / createOpenaiTranscription(model, apiKey, config?)","level":3},{"id":"openaivideo-model-config-createopenaivideo-model-apikey-config","text":"openaiVideo(model, config?) / createOpenaiVideo(model, apiKey, config?)","level":3},{"id":"openaidecider-model-config-createopenaidecider-model-apikey-config","text":"openaiDecider(model, config?) / createOpenaiDecider(model, apiKey, config?)","level":3},{"id":"openairealtime-openairealtimetoken","text":"openaiRealtime(...) / openaiRealtimeToken(...)","level":3},{"id":"next-steps","text":"Next Steps","level":2},{"id":"provider-tools","text":"Provider Tools","level":2},{"id":"websearchtool","text":"webSearchTool","level":3},{"id":"websearchpreviewtool","text":"webSearchPreviewTool","level":3},{"id":"filesearchtool","text":"fileSearchTool","level":3},{"id":"imagegenerationtool","text":"imageGenerationTool","level":3},{"id":"codeinterpretertool","text":"codeInterpreterTool","level":3},{"id":"mcptool","text":"mcpTool","level":3},{"id":"computerusetool","text":"computerUseTool","level":3},{"id":"localshelltool","text":"localShellTool","level":3},{"id":"shelltool","text":"shellTool","level":3},{"id":"attaching-hosted-skills","text":"Attaching hosted skills","level":4},{"id":"applypatchtool","text":"applyPatchTool","level":3},{"id":"customtool","text":"customTool","level":3}]},"frameworks":["react","vue","solid","svelte","preact","angular","vanilla","octane"],"downloadMarkdown":"\nThe OpenAI adapter provides access to OpenAI's models, including GPT-4o, GPT-5, image generation (DALL-E), text-to-speech (TTS), and audio transcription (Whisper).\n\n> Using a third-party provider that speaks the OpenAI API (DeepSeek, Moonshot/Kimi, Together, Fireworks, a local LM Studio/vLLM server, …)? See the [OpenAI-Compatible Adapter](./openai-compatible) for a generic `openaiCompatible({ baseURL, apiKey, models })` factory.\n\n## Installation\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"package-manager\" mode=\"install\" -->\n\nreact: @tanstack/ai-openai\nvue: @tanstack/ai-openai\nsolid: @tanstack/ai-openai\nsvelte: @tanstack/ai-openai\npreact: @tanstack/ai-openai\nangular: @tanstack/ai-openai\nvanilla: @tanstack/ai-openai\noctane: @tanstack/ai-openai\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\n## Basic Usage\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiText } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: openaiText(\"gpt-5.2\"),\n  messages: [{ role: \"user\", content: \"Hello!\" }],\n});\n```\n\n## Chat Completions API\n\n`@tanstack/ai-openai` ships two text adapters that hit different OpenAI endpoints. `openaiText` (default) calls the Responses API (`/v1/responses`). `openaiChatCompletions` calls the older Chat Completions API (`/v1/chat/completions`).\n\nPick whichever fits your wire format and feature needs:\n\n| | `openaiText` (Responses) | `openaiChatCompletions` (Chat Completions) |\n|---|---|---|\n| Endpoint | `/v1/responses` | `/v1/chat/completions` |\n| Reasoning summaries | Yes — set `modelOptions.reasoning.summary: 'auto'` to surface reasoning text via `REASONING_*` events | No — reasoning tokens are still consumed but cannot be exposed |\n| Wire-format compatibility | OpenAI-only | Matches the older de-facto industry shape (Grok, Groq, OpenRouter, many local model servers) |\n| Structured output streaming | `text.format: { type: 'json_schema', strict: true }` + `stream: true` | `response_format: { type: 'json_schema', strict: true }` + `stream: true` |\n\nUse `openaiText` when you want reasoning-summary streaming or OpenAI-specific Responses features. Use `openaiChatCompletions` when you're migrating off a Chat-Completions-style provider, share request-building code with other Chat-Completions adapters in your stack, or want the more battle-tested wire format.\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiChatCompletions } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: openaiChatCompletions(\"gpt-5.2\"),\n  messages: [{ role: \"user\", content: \"Hello!\" }],\n});\n```\n\nWith an explicit API key:\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { createOpenaiChatCompletions } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\n\nconst adapter = createOpenaiChatCompletions(\"gpt-5.2\", process.env.OPENAI_API_KEY!, {\n  // organization, baseURL, headers — all optional\n});\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter,\n  messages: [{ role: \"user\", content: \"Hello!\" }],\n});\n```\n\nBoth adapters work identically with [Structured Outputs](../structured-outputs/overview) — including `stream: true` — and accept the same `modelOptions` (temperature, top_p, max_tokens, stop, …). The reasoning section below applies to `openaiText`; `openaiChatCompletions` accepts `modelOptions.reasoning.effort` but cannot stream summary text.\n\n## Basic Usage - Custom API Key\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { createOpenaiChat } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\n\nconst adapter = createOpenaiChat(\"gpt-5.2\", process.env.OPENAI_API_KEY!, {\n  // ... your config options\n});\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter,\n  messages: [{ role: \"user\", content: \"Hello!\" }],\n});\n```\n\n## Sign in with ChatGPT (BYOK)\n\nMany of your users have a ChatGPT plan but no API key. Let them sign in with ChatGPT. The token bills their ChatGPT plan, not your account.\n\nThe helpers in `@tanstack/ai-openai/siwc` put the access token into the `openai` [BYOK](../advanced/byok) slot. Your relay reads it like a pasted key.\n\nBefore you start, check these limits:\n\n- OpenAI allows this sign-in only for open-source and locally hosted apps. For a hosted app, fill in the [interest form](https://openai.com/form/sign-in-with-chatgpt-interest/).\n- OpenAI redirects only to `127.0.0.1`. Something must answer on that address. Vite listens on `::1` by default. The `ts-react-chat` example runs a small script on `127.0.0.1:3000` that redirects to `localhost:3000`.\n- Keep the app on `localhost`, because passkey storage does not work on an IP address. The callback lands on `127.0.0.1`, then `completeChatGptSignIn` sends the browser back to `localhost`.\n- The callback page must be at `/auth/callback`.\n\n### 1. Add the sign-in button\n\nCall `startChatGptSignIn` from a click. `agentName` is your app name. OpenAI shows it on the consent screen.\n\n```tsx\nimport { startChatGptSignIn } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai/siwc\";\n\nexport function ChatGptButton() {\n  return (\n    <button\n      type=\"button\"\n      onClick={() => {\n        void startChatGptSignIn({ agentName: \"My App\" });\n      }}\n    >\n      Continue with ChatGPT\n    </button>\n  );\n}\n```\n\n### 2. Finish on `/auth/callback`\n\nRender this component on the `/auth/callback` route. It exchanges the code when the page loads. Then the user clicks to save.\n\n```tsx\nimport { useEffect, useRef, useState } from \"react\";\nimport {\n  completeChatGptSignIn,\n  saveChatGptSignIn,\n} from \"@tanstack/ai-openai/siwc\";\nimport type { ChatGptSignIn } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai/siwc\";\nimport { byok } from \"./byok\";\n\nexport function ChatGptCallback() {\n  const started = useRef(false);\n  const [signIn, setSignIn] = useState<ChatGptSignIn | null>(null);\n  const [error, setError] = useState(\"\");\n\n  useEffect(() => {\n    // The code works one time. Strict Mode runs effects two times.\n    if (started.current) return;\n    started.current = true;\n    completeChatGptSignIn().then(setSignIn, (caught: unknown) => {\n      setError(caught instanceof Error ? caught.message : \"Sign-in failed\");\n    });\n  }, []);\n\n  if (error) return <p>{error}</p>;\n  if (!signIn) return <p>Finishing sign-in...</p>;\n  return (\n    <button\n      type=\"button\"\n      onClick={() => {\n        void saveChatGptSignIn(byok, signIn);\n      }}\n    >\n      Save ChatGPT sign-in\n    </button>\n  );\n}\n```\n\nThe save needs a click because passkey storage shows a browser prompt. The refresh token goes into a second keyring slot. No send attaches that slot, so the refresh token stays in the browser.\n\n### 3. Refresh the token\n\nThe access token lasts one hour. Call `refreshChatGptSignIn` on a timer:\n\n```tsx\nimport { useEffect } from \"react\";\nimport { refreshChatGptSignIn } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai/siwc\";\nimport { byok } from \"./byok\";\n\nexport function useChatGptRefresh() {\n  useEffect(() => {\n    const refresh = () => {\n      refreshChatGptSignIn(byok).catch(console.error);\n    };\n    refresh();\n    const timer = setInterval(refresh, 60_000);\n    return () => clearInterval(timer);\n  }, []);\n}\n```\n\nThe call does nothing until the token has less than five minutes left. If OpenAI rejects the refresh token, the call clears the sign-in. Then the user must sign in again.\n\n### 4. Read the token on the relay\n\nThe relay code is the same as for a pasted key. Add `store: false`, because the ChatGPT route requires it.\n\n```typescript\nimport {\n  chat,\n  chatParamsFromRequest,\n  toServerSentEventsResponse,\n} from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { createOpenaiChat } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\nimport { openaiByok } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai/byok\";\nimport { byokMissing, getByokKey } from \"@tanstack/ai/byok/server\";\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const params = await chatParamsFromRequest(request);\n  const apiKey = getByokKey(request, openaiByok);\n  if (!apiKey) return byokMissing(openaiByok);\n\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: createOpenaiChat(\"gpt-6-astra\", apiKey),\n    messages: params.messages,\n    threadId: params.threadId,\n    runId: params.runId,\n    modelOptions: { store: false },\n  });\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream);\n}\n```\n\n`store: false` also works with an API key. A ChatGPT token does not start with `sk-`, so use that test if you must send different options.\n\nThe ChatGPT route has these limits:\n\n- Use a model that the user's ChatGPT plan includes.\n- Do not send `temperature`, `top_p`, `max_output_tokens`, `metadata`, or `previous_response_id`.\n- Hosted tools do not work. This includes image generation, file search, code interpreter, computer use, and hosted MCP.\n- Audio input and transcription do not work.\n\nClick **Continue with ChatGPT**, approve, save, then send a message. The relay calls OpenAI on the user's ChatGPT plan.\n\nThe `ts-react-chat` example has this flow in its key dialog.\n\n## Configuration\n\n```typescript\nimport { createOpenaiChat, type OpenAITextConfig } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\n\nconst config: Omit<OpenAITextConfig, \"apiKey\"> = {\n  organization: \"org-...\", // Optional\n  baseURL: \"https://api.openai.com/v1\", // Optional, for custom endpoints\n};\n\nconst adapter = createOpenaiChat(\"gpt-5.2\", process.env.OPENAI_API_KEY!, config);\n```\n\n### Tools that cannot use strict mode\n\nOpenAI holds tool arguments to the schema only when the tool is sent with `strict: true`. Some schemas cannot be strict, for example a schema that uses `$ref`, `z.any()`, or `z.record()`. The adapter sends these tools with `strict: false`, so the tool still works. The model can then return arguments that do not match the schema.\n\nIn development, the adapter logs a warning once for each of these tools:\n\n```txt\ntool \"lookup_user\" sent with strict: false: schema uses $ref, which strict mode does not support\n```\n\nTo get strict mode back, change the schema so that the reason goes away. If you accept a non-strict tool, turn the warning off in the adapter config:\n\n```typescript\nimport { createOpenaiChat } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\n\nconst adapter = createOpenaiChat(\"gpt-6-astra\", process.env.OPENAI_API_KEY!, {\n  strictFallbackWarning: false,\n});\n```\n\nThe warning never runs when `NODE_ENV` is `production`. The same option works on every adapter built on the OpenAI API, for example Groq, Bedrock, and Vercel AI Gateway.\n \n## Example: Chat Completion\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat, toServerSentEventsResponse } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiText } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const { messages } = await request.json();\n\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: openaiText(\"gpt-5.2\"),\n    messages,\n  });\n\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream);\n}\n```\n\n## Example: With Tools\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat, toServerSentEventsResponse, toolDefinition } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiText } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\nimport { z } from \"zod\";\n\nconst getWeatherDef = toolDefinition({\n  name: \"get_weather\",\n  description: \"Get the current weather\",\n  inputSchema: z.object({\n    location: z.string(),\n  }),\n});\n\nconst getWeather = getWeatherDef.server(async ({ location }) => {\n  // Fetch weather data\n  return { temperature: 72, conditions: \"sunny\" };\n});\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const { messages } = await request.json();\n\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: openaiText(\"gpt-5.2\"),\n    messages,\n    tools: [getWeather],\n  });\n\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream);\n}\n```\n\n## Model Options\n\nOpenAI supports various provider-specific options. Sampling parameters live here too — `temperature`, `top_p`, and `max_output_tokens` (the Responses API token-limit key) — rather than as root-level props on `chat()`:\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiText } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: openaiText(\"gpt-5.2\"),\n  messages: [{ role: \"user\", content: \"Hello!\" }],\n  modelOptions: {\n    temperature: 0.7,\n    max_output_tokens: 1000,\n    top_p: 0.9,\n  },\n});\n```\n\n> The `openaiChatCompletions` adapter targets `/v1/chat/completions`, where the token-limit key is `max_tokens` (not `max_output_tokens`). If you previously passed `temperature` / `topP` / `maxTokens` at the root of `chat()`, see [Moving Sampling Options into modelOptions](../migration/sampling-options-to-model-options).\n\n### Reasoning\n\nEnable reasoning for models that support it (e.g., GPT-5, O3). This allows the model to show its reasoning process, which is streamed as `thinking` chunks:\n\n```typescript ignore\nmodelOptions: {\n  reasoning: {\n    effort: \"medium\", // \"none\" | \"minimal\" | \"low\" | \"medium\" | \"high\"\n    summary: \"detailed\", // \"auto\" | \"detailed\" (optional)\n  },\n}\n```\n\nWhen reasoning is enabled, the model's reasoning process is streamed separately from the response text and appears as a collapsible thinking section in the UI.\n\n## Summarization\n\nSummarize long text content:\n\n```typescript\nimport { summarize } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiSummarize } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\n\nconst result = await summarize({\n  adapter: openaiSummarize(\"gpt-5-mini\"),\n  text: \"Your long text to summarize...\",\n  maxLength: 100,\n  style: \"concise\", // \"concise\" | \"bullet-points\" | \"paragraph\"\n});\n\nconsole.log(result.summary);\n```\n\n## Embeddings\n\nGenerate embedding vectors with the text-embedding-3 models:\n\n```typescript\nimport { embed } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiEmbedding } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\n\nconst result = await embed({\n  adapter: openaiEmbedding(\"text-embedding-3-small\"),\n  input: [\"a red guitar\", \"a blue drum kit\"],\n});\n\nconsole.log(result.embeddings[0]?.vector);\nconsole.log(result.usage?.promptTokens);\n```\n\nBoth models support Matryoshka dimension reduction via the top-level `dimensions` option:\n\n```typescript\nimport { embed } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiEmbedding } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\n\nconst result = await embed({\n  adapter: openaiEmbedding(\"text-embedding-3-large\"),\n  input: \"a red guitar\",\n  dimensions: 1024,\n});\n```\n\nSee the [Embeddings guide](../embeddings.md) for the full API.\n\n## Image Generation\n\nGenerate images:\n\n```typescript\nimport { generateImage } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiImage } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\n\nconst result = await generateImage({\n  adapter: openaiImage(\"gpt-image-2\"),\n  prompt: \"A futuristic cityscape at sunset\",\n  numberOfImages: 1,\n  size: \"1024x1024\",\n});\n\nconsole.log(result.images);\n```\n\n### Image Model Options\n\n```typescript\nimport { generateImage } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiImage } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\n\nconst result = await generateImage({\n  adapter: openaiImage(\"gpt-image-2\"),\n  prompt: \"...\",\n  modelOptions: {\n    quality: \"high\", // \"high\" | \"medium\" | \"low\" | \"auto\"\n  },\n});\n```\n\n## Text-to-Speech\n\nGenerate speech from text:\n\n```typescript\nimport { generateSpeech } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiSpeech } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\n\nconst result = await generateSpeech({\n  adapter: openaiSpeech(\"tts-1\"),\n  text: \"Hello, welcome to TanStack AI!\",\n  voice: \"alloy\",\n  format: \"mp3\",\n});\n\n// result.audio contains base64-encoded audio\nconsole.log(result.format); // \"mp3\"\n```\n\n### TTS Voices\n\nAvailable voices: `alloy`, `echo`, `fable`, `onyx`, `nova`, `shimmer`, `ash`, `ballad`, `coral`, `sage`, `verse`\n\n### TTS Model Options\n\n```typescript\nimport { generateSpeech } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiSpeech } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\n\nconst result = await generateSpeech({\n  adapter: openaiSpeech(\"tts-1-hd\"),\n  text: \"High quality speech\",\n  modelOptions: {\n    instructions: \"Speak slowly and clearly.\", // voice instructions (not supported by tts-1/tts-1-hd)\n  },\n});\n```\n\n## Transcription\n\nTranscribe audio to text:\n\n```typescript\nimport { generateTranscription } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiTranscription } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\nimport { audioFile } from \"./audio\";\n\nconst result = await generateTranscription({\n  adapter: openaiTranscription(\"whisper-1\"),\n  audio: audioFile, // File object or base64 string\n  language: \"en\",\n});\n\nconsole.log(result.text); // Transcribed text\n```\n\n### Transcription Model Options\n\n```typescript\nimport { generateTranscription } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiTranscription } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\nimport { audioFile } from \"./audio\";\n\nconst result = await generateTranscription({\n  adapter: openaiTranscription(\"whisper-1\"),\n  audio: audioFile,\n  responseFormat: \"verbose_json\",\n  prompt: \"Technical terms: API, SDK\",\n  modelOptions: {\n    temperature: 0,\n    timestamp_granularities: [\"word\", \"segment\"],\n  },\n});\n\n// Access the transcribed text\nconsole.log(result.text);\n```\n\n### Speaker Diarization\n\nUse `gpt-4o-transcribe-diarize` for speaker-labeled transcripts:\n\n```typescript\nimport { generateTranscription } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiTranscription } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\nimport { meetingAudioFile } from \"./audio\";\n\nconst result = await generateTranscription({\n  adapter: openaiTranscription(\"gpt-4o-transcribe-diarize\"),\n  audio: meetingAudioFile,\n  modelOptions: {\n    known_speaker_names: [\"agent\", \"customer\"],\n    known_speaker_references: [\n      \"data:audio/wav;base64,...\",\n      \"data:audio/wav;base64,...\",\n    ],\n  },\n});\n\nfor (const segment of result.segments ?? []) {\n  console.log(segment.speaker, segment.start, segment.end, segment.text);\n}\n```\n\nWhen no response format is specified, `gpt-4o-transcribe-diarize` requests default to `response_format: \"diarized_json\"` and `chunking_strategy: \"auto\"`; passing a top-level `responseFormat` of `\"json\"` or `\"text\"` opts out of speaker segments. `known_speaker_names` and `known_speaker_references` must be provided together (up to 4, matching lengths). OpenAI does not support `prompt`, `include`, or `timestamp_granularities` with diarized transcription.\n\n## Evaluate\n\nSometimes you need an answer that your code can branch on, not chat text. Examples are a queue name, an urgency level, or a yes or no.\nUse `openaiDecider` with `decide()` to ask typed questions about one shared `state`. The adapter calls the OpenAI Decisions API (`/v1/decisions`):\n\n```typescript\nimport { decide, choice, score, boolean } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiDecider } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\n\nconst ticket = {\n  subject: \"Charged twice for the same invoice\",\n  body: \"Please refund the extra payment.\",\n};\n\nconst result = await decide({\n  adapter: openaiDecider(\"gpt-6-luna\"),\n  state: ticket,\n  questions: {\n    queue: choice({\n      instructions: \"Which team should handle this ticket?\",\n      options: {\n        billing: \"Payments, invoices, refunds\",\n        tech: \"Bugs, outages, integrations\",\n        sales: \"Pricing, upgrades, new accounts\",\n      },\n    }),\n    urgency: score({\n      instructions: \"How urgent is this ticket?\",\n      levels: [\"low\", \"medium\", \"high\"],\n    }),\n    refund: boolean({\n      instructions: \"Is the customer asking for a refund?\",\n    }),\n  },\n});\n\nconsole.log(result.queue.value); // \"billing\"\nconsole.log(result.urgency.value); // \"medium\"\nconsole.log(result.refund.value); // true\nconsole.log(result.meta.usage);\n```\n\n`openaiDecider` reads `OPENAI_API_KEY` from the environment. To pass a key yourself, use `createOpenaiDecider(\"gpt-6-luna\", \"sk-...\")`.\n\nGood to know:\n\n- `gpt-6-luna` is the only Decisions model.\n- An object `state` goes to OpenAI as JSON text.\n- If OpenAI refuses to answer a question, `decide()` throws an error with the name of that question.\n- `boolean()` criteria work. The adapter adds the true and false meanings to the instructions.\n\nSee the [Evaluate guide](../evaluate/evaluate) for question helpers, the result shape, abort, and middleware.\n\n## Environment Variables\n\nSet your API key in environment variables:\n\n```bash\nOPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...\n```\n\n## API Reference\n\nEvery factory pair follows the same shape: the short factory (`openaiText`, `openaiImage`, …) reads `OPENAI_API_KEY` from the environment, while the `create*` variant takes an explicit API key. Both take `model` as the first argument.\n\n### `openaiText(model, config?)`\n\nCreates an OpenAI text adapter against the Responses API (`/v1/responses`) using `OPENAI_API_KEY` from the environment.\n\n**Parameters:**\n\n- `model` - OpenAI chat model id (e.g. `\"gpt-5.2\"`, `\"gpt-4o-mini\"`)\n- `config?.organization` - Organization ID (optional)\n- `config?.baseURL` - Custom base URL (optional)\n\n### `createOpenaiChat(model, apiKey, config?)`\n\nCreates an OpenAI text adapter (Responses API) with an explicit API key.\n\n### `openaiChatCompletions(model, config?)`\n\nCreates an OpenAI text adapter that targets `/v1/chat/completions` instead of the Responses API. See [Chat Completions API](#chat-completions-api) for when to use this over `openaiText`.\n\n### `createOpenaiChatCompletions(model, apiKey, config?)`\n\nCreates an OpenAI chat-completions adapter with an explicit API key.\n\n### `openaiSummarize(model, config?)` / `createOpenaiSummarize(model, apiKey, config?)`\n\nCreates an OpenAI summarization adapter.\n\n### `openaiImage(model, config?)` / `createOpenaiImage(model, apiKey, config?)`\n\nCreates an OpenAI image generation adapter (DALL-E, gpt-image).\n\n### `openaiSpeech(model, config?)` / `createOpenaiSpeech(model, apiKey, config?)`\n\nCreates an OpenAI text-to-speech adapter.\n\n### `openaiTranscription(model, config?)` / `createOpenaiTranscription(model, apiKey, config?)`\n\nCreates an OpenAI transcription adapter for Whisper, GPT-4o transcription, and GPT-4o diarized transcription models.\n\n### `openaiVideo(model, config?)` / `createOpenaiVideo(model, apiKey, config?)`\n\nCreates an OpenAI video generation adapter (Sora). _Experimental._\n\n### `openaiDecider(model, config?)` / `createOpenaiDecider(model, apiKey, config?)`\n\nCreates an OpenAI evaluate adapter for `decide()`. See [Evaluate](#evaluate) for usage.\n\n### `openaiRealtime(...)` / `openaiRealtimeToken(...)`\n\nRealtime voice adapters. See [Realtime Voice Chat](../media/realtime-chat) for usage.\n\n## Next Steps\n\n- [Getting Started](../getting-started/quick-start) - Learn the basics\n- [Tools Guide](../tools/tools) - Learn about tools\n- [Other Adapters](./anthropic) - Explore other providers\n\n## Provider Tools\n\nOpenAI exposes several native tools beyond user-defined function calls.\nImport them from `@tanstack/ai-openai/tools` and pass them into\n`chat({ tools: [...] })`.\n\n> For the full concept, a comparison matrix, and type-gating details, see\n> [Provider Tools](../tools/provider-tools.md).\n\n### `webSearchTool`\n\nEnables the model to run a web search and return grounded results with\ncitations. Pass a `WebSearchToolConfig` object (typed from the OpenAI SDK)\nto configure the tool.\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiText } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\nimport { webSearchTool } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai/tools\";\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: openaiText(\"gpt-5.2\"),\n  messages: [{ role: \"user\", content: \"What's new in AI this week?\" }],\n  tools: [webSearchTool({ type: \"web_search\" })],\n});\n```\n\n**Supported models:** GPT-4o, GPT-5, and Responses API-capable models. See [Provider Tools](../tools/provider-tools.md#which-models-support-which-tools).\n\n### `webSearchPreviewTool`\n\nThe preview variant of web search with additional options for controlling\nsearch context size and user location. Use this when you want fine-grained\ncontrol over the search context sent to the model.\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiText } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\nimport { webSearchPreviewTool } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai/tools\";\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: openaiText(\"gpt-5.2\"),\n  messages: [{ role: \"user\", content: \"Latest news about TypeScript\" }],\n  tools: [\n    webSearchPreviewTool({\n      type: \"web_search_preview_2025_03_11\",\n      search_context_size: \"high\",\n    }),\n  ],\n});\n```\n\n**Supported models:** GPT-4o and above. See [Provider Tools](../tools/provider-tools.md#which-models-support-which-tools).\n\nWhen the model uses hosted web search, the assistant tool-call part includes\n`metadata.providerExecuted: true` and the normalized `metadata.sources` array.\nOpenAI's raw search call and URL citations stay under `metadata.openai`. The\nagent loop does not execute this call in your application, and the adapter\nreplays the raw response items on the next turn.\n\n### `fileSearchTool`\n\nSearches OpenAI vector stores that you have pre-populated, letting the model\nretrieve relevant document chunks. Provide the `vector_store_ids` to search\nand optionally limit results with `max_num_results` (1–50).\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiText } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\nimport { fileSearchTool } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai/tools\";\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: openaiText(\"gpt-5.2\"),\n  messages: [{ role: \"user\", content: \"What does the handbook say about PTO?\" }],\n  tools: [\n    fileSearchTool({\n      type: \"file_search\",\n      vector_store_ids: [\"vs_abc123\"],\n      max_num_results: 5,\n    }),\n  ],\n});\n```\n\n**Supported models:** GPT-4o and above. See [Provider Tools](../tools/provider-tools.md#which-models-support-which-tools).\n\n### `imageGenerationTool`\n\nAllows the model to generate images inline during a conversation using\nDALL-E/GPT-Image. Pass quality, size, and style options via the config object.\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiText } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\nimport { imageGenerationTool } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai/tools\";\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: openaiText(\"gpt-5.2\"),\n  messages: [{ role: \"user\", content: \"Draw a logo for my app\" }],\n  tools: [\n    imageGenerationTool({\n      quality: \"high\",\n      size: \"1024x1024\",\n    }),\n  ],\n});\n```\n\n**Supported models:** GPT-5 and GPT-Image-capable models. See [Provider Tools](../tools/provider-tools.md#which-models-support-which-tools).\n\n### `codeInterpreterTool`\n\nGives the model a sandboxed Python execution environment. The `container`\nfield configures the execution environment; pass the full\n`CodeInterpreterToolConfig` object.\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiText } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\nimport { codeInterpreterTool } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai/tools\";\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: openaiText(\"gpt-5.2\"),\n  messages: [{ role: \"user\", content: \"Analyse this CSV and plot a chart\" }],\n  tools: [\n    codeInterpreterTool({ type: \"code_interpreter\", container: { type: \"auto\" } }),\n  ],\n});\n```\n\n**Supported models:** GPT-4o and above. See [Provider Tools](../tools/provider-tools.md#which-models-support-which-tools).\n\n### `mcpTool`\n\nConnects the model to a remote MCP (Model Context Protocol) server, exposing\nall its capabilities as callable tools. Provide either `server_url` or\n`connector_id` — not both.\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiText } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\nimport { mcpTool } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai/tools\";\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: openaiText(\"gpt-5.2\"),\n  messages: [{ role: \"user\", content: \"List my GitHub issues\" }],\n  tools: [\n    mcpTool({\n      server_url: \"https://mcp.example.com\",\n      server_label: \"github\",\n    }),\n  ],\n});\n```\n\n**Supported models:** GPT-4o and above. See [Provider Tools](../tools/provider-tools.md#which-models-support-which-tools).\n\n### `computerUseTool`\n\nLets the model observe a virtual desktop via screenshots and interact with\nit using keyboard and mouse events. Provide the display dimensions and the\nexecution environment type.\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiText } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\nimport { computerUseTool } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai/tools\";\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: openaiText(\"computer-use-preview\"),\n  messages: [{ role: \"user\", content: \"Open Chrome and navigate to example.com\" }],\n  tools: [\n    computerUseTool({\n      type: \"computer_use_preview\",\n      display_width: 1024,\n      display_height: 768,\n      environment: \"browser\",\n    }),\n  ],\n});\n```\n\n**Supported models:** `computer-use-preview`. See [Provider Tools](../tools/provider-tools.md#which-models-support-which-tools).\n\n### `localShellTool`\n\nThe model returns a `local_shell` tool call. Your app runs the command. Then your app sends the output back on the next request. `localShellTool()` takes no arguments. Add it to `tools`.\n\nMatch `toolName` on `TOOL_CALL_START`. Read `input` on the `TOOL_CALL_END` with the same `toolCallId`. `input.command` is the command. `input.env` is the environment variables.\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiText } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\nimport { localShellTool } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai/tools\";\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: openaiText(\"gpt-5.6\"),\n  messages: [{ role: \"user\", content: \"Run the test suite and summarise failures\" }],\n  tools: [localShellTool()],\n});\n\nlet localShellCallId: string | undefined;\nfor await (const chunk of stream) {\n  if (chunk.type === \"TOOL_CALL_START\" && chunk.toolName === \"local_shell\") {\n    localShellCallId = chunk.toolCallId;\n  }\n  if (chunk.type === \"TOOL_CALL_END\" && chunk.toolCallId === localShellCallId) {\n    console.log(chunk.input);\n  }\n}\n```\n\nSend the command output as the tool result. Use `{ output: string }`, or a string. The next request sends `local_shell_call_output`.\n\n**Supported models:** GPT-5.x and other agent-capable models. See [Provider Tools](../tools/provider-tools.md#which-models-support-which-tools).\n\n### `shellTool`\n\n`shellTool()` gives the model a shell. A container environment runs on OpenAI. A local environment runs in your app.\n\nWhen your app must run the commands, pass `environment: { type: \"local\" }`. Match `toolName` on `TOOL_CALL_START`. Read `input` on the `TOOL_CALL_END` with the same `toolCallId`. `input.commands` is the command list. `input.timeout_ms` is the time limit. `input.max_output_length` is the output limit.\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiText } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\nimport { shellTool } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai/tools\";\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: openaiText(\"gpt-5.6\"),\n  messages: [{ role: \"user\", content: \"Count lines in all JS files\" }],\n  tools: [shellTool({ environment: { type: \"local\" } })],\n});\n\nlet shellCallId: string | undefined;\nfor await (const chunk of stream) {\n  if (chunk.type === \"TOOL_CALL_START\" && chunk.toolName === \"shell\") {\n    shellCallId = chunk.toolCallId;\n  }\n  if (chunk.type === \"TOOL_CALL_END\" && chunk.toolCallId === shellCallId) {\n    console.log(chunk.input);\n  }\n}\n```\n\nReturn one result per command:\n\n```typescript\nconst shellResult = {\n  output: [\n    {\n      stdout: \"12\\n\",\n      stderr: \"\",\n      outcome: { type: \"exit\" as const, exit_code: 0 },\n    },\n  ],\n};\n```\n\n`outcome.type` is `\"exit\"` or `\"timeout\"`. The next request sends `shell_call_output`. If the same response has no `shell_call_output`, a shell call with no environment comes back to your app.\n\nA container environment does not come back as a tool call. Pass `environment` to attach that container and hosted skills.\n\n**Supported models:** GPT-5.x and other agent-capable models. Responses API\nonly — Chat Completions does not support the shell tool. See [Provider Tools](../tools/provider-tools.md#which-models-support-which-tools).\n\n#### Attaching hosted skills\n\nPass `environment.skills` to load provider-managed skill bundles into the\nshell's container (Responses API only).\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat, toServerSentEventsResponse } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiText } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\nimport { shellTool } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai/tools\";\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const { messages } = await request.json();\n\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: openaiText(\"gpt-5.2\"),\n    messages,\n    tools: [\n      shellTool({\n        environment: {\n          type: \"container_auto\",\n          skills: [\n            { type: \"skill_reference\", skill_id: \"skill_abc\", version: \"2\" },\n          ],\n        },\n      }),\n    ],\n  });\n\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream);\n}\n```\n\nFor the full reference — skill shape, `version` string format, and the\nAnthropic equivalent — see [Provider Skills](../tools/provider-skills.md).\n\n### `applyPatchTool`\n\nThe model returns an `apply_patch` tool call. Your app applies the diff. Then your app sends the result back. `applyPatchTool()` takes no arguments. Add it to `tools`.\n\nMatch `toolName` on `TOOL_CALL_START`. Read `input` on the `TOOL_CALL_END` with the same `toolCallId`. `input.operation` is one file change. `operation.type` is `create_file`, `update_file`, or `delete_file`. `operation.path` is the file path. `create_file` and `update_file` also include `operation.diff`.\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiText } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\nimport { applyPatchTool } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai/tools\";\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: openaiText(\"gpt-5.6\"),\n  messages: [{ role: \"user\", content: \"Fix the import paths in src/index.ts\" }],\n  tools: [applyPatchTool()],\n});\n\nlet patchCallId: string | undefined;\nfor await (const chunk of stream) {\n  if (chunk.type === \"TOOL_CALL_START\" && chunk.toolName === \"apply_patch\") {\n    patchCallId = chunk.toolCallId;\n  }\n  if (chunk.type === \"TOOL_CALL_END\" && chunk.toolCallId === patchCallId) {\n    console.log(chunk.input);\n  }\n}\n```\n\nSend this object as the tool result. The next request sends `apply_patch_call_output`.\n\n```typescript\nconst patchResult = {\n  status: \"completed\" as const,\n  output: \"Updated src/index.ts\",\n};\n```\n\nIf the patch fails, set `status` to `\"failed\"`. Put the error text in `output`. Keep `applyPatchTool()` in `tools` on the next request. A patch-only turn has no text. If you use `chat({ stream: false })`, `text` is empty. Read the `apply_patch` tool call from `chunks` with the same checks as the loop above.\n\n**Supported models:** GPT-5.x and other agent-capable models. See [Provider Tools](../tools/provider-tools.md#which-models-support-which-tools).\n\n### `customTool`\n\nDefines a custom Responses API tool with an explicit name, description, and\nformat. Use this when none of the structured tool types fits your use case.\nUnlike branded provider tools, `customTool` returns a plain `Tool` and is\naccepted by any chat model.\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiText } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\nimport { customTool } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai/tools\";\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: openaiText(\"gpt-5.2\"),\n  messages: [{ role: \"user\", content: \"Look up order #1234\" }],\n  tools: [\n    customTool({\n      type: \"custom\",\n      name: \"lookup_order\",\n      description: \"Look up the status of a customer order by order ID\",\n    }),\n  ],\n});\n```\n\n**Supported models:** all Responses API models. See [Provider Tools](../tools/provider-tools.md#which-models-support-which-tools).\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: OpenAI\nid: openai-adapter\norder: 1\ndescription: \"Use OpenAI models with TanStack AI — GPT-4o, GPT-5, DALL-E image generation, TTS, and Whisper transcription via @tanstack/ai-openai.\"\nkeywords:\n  - tanstack ai\n  - openai\n  - gpt-4o\n  - gpt-5\n  - dall-e\n  - whisper\n  - openai tts\n  - adapter\n  - chatgpt\n---\n\nThe OpenAI adapter provides access to OpenAI's models, including GPT-4o, GPT-5, image generation (DALL-E), text-to-speech (TTS), and audio transcription (Whisper).\n\n> Using a third-party provider that speaks the OpenAI API (DeepSeek, Moonshot/Kimi, Together, Fireworks, a local LM Studio/vLLM server, …)? See the [OpenAI-Compatible Adapter](./openai-compatible) for a generic `openaiCompatible({ baseURL, apiKey, models })` factory.\n\n## Installation\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"package-manager\" mode=\"install\" -->\n\nreact: @tanstack/ai-openai\nvue: @tanstack/ai-openai\nsolid: @tanstack/ai-openai\nsvelte: @tanstack/ai-openai\npreact: @tanstack/ai-openai\nangular: @tanstack/ai-openai\nvanilla: @tanstack/ai-openai\noctane: @tanstack/ai-openai\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\n## Basic Usage\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiText } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: openaiText(\"gpt-5.2\"),\n  messages: [{ role: \"user\", content: \"Hello!\" }],\n});\n```\n\n## Chat Completions API\n\n`@tanstack/ai-openai` ships two text adapters that hit different OpenAI endpoints. `openaiText` (default) calls the Responses API (`/v1/responses`). `openaiChatCompletions` calls the older Chat Completions API (`/v1/chat/completions`).\n\nPick whichever fits your wire format and feature needs:\n\n| | `openaiText` (Responses) | `openaiChatCompletions` (Chat Completions) |\n|---|---|---|\n| Endpoint | `/v1/responses` | `/v1/chat/completions` |\n| Reasoning summaries | Yes — set `modelOptions.reasoning.summary: 'auto'` to surface reasoning text via `REASONING_*` events | No — reasoning tokens are still consumed but cannot be exposed |\n| Wire-format compatibility | OpenAI-only | Matches the older de-facto industry shape (Grok, Groq, OpenRouter, many local model servers) |\n| Structured output streaming | `text.format: { type: 'json_schema', strict: true }` + `stream: true` | `response_format: { type: 'json_schema', strict: true }` + `stream: true` |\n\nUse `openaiText` when you want reasoning-summary streaming or OpenAI-specific Responses features. Use `openaiChatCompletions` when you're migrating off a Chat-Completions-style provider, share request-building code with other Chat-Completions adapters in your stack, or want the more battle-tested wire format.\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiChatCompletions } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: openaiChatCompletions(\"gpt-5.2\"),\n  messages: [{ role: \"user\", content: \"Hello!\" }],\n});\n```\n\nWith an explicit API key:\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { createOpenaiChatCompletions } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\n\nconst adapter = createOpenaiChatCompletions(\"gpt-5.2\", process.env.OPENAI_API_KEY!, {\n  // organization, baseURL, headers — all optional\n});\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter,\n  messages: [{ role: \"user\", content: \"Hello!\" }],\n});\n```\n\nBoth adapters work identically with [Structured Outputs](../structured-outputs/overview) — including `stream: true` — and accept the same `modelOptions` (temperature, top_p, max_tokens, stop, …). The reasoning section below applies to `openaiText`; `openaiChatCompletions` accepts `modelOptions.reasoning.effort` but cannot stream summary text.\n\n## Basic Usage - Custom API Key\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { createOpenaiChat } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\n\nconst adapter = createOpenaiChat(\"gpt-5.2\", process.env.OPENAI_API_KEY!, {\n  // ... your config options\n});\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter,\n  messages: [{ role: \"user\", content: \"Hello!\" }],\n});\n```\n\n## Sign in with ChatGPT (BYOK)\n\nMany of your users have a ChatGPT plan but no API key. Let them sign in with ChatGPT. The token bills their ChatGPT plan, not your account.\n\nThe helpers in `@tanstack/ai-openai/siwc` put the access token into the `openai` [BYOK](../advanced/byok) slot. Your relay reads it like a pasted key.\n\nBefore you start, check these limits:\n\n- OpenAI allows this sign-in only for open-source and locally hosted apps. For a hosted app, fill in the [interest form](https://openai.com/form/sign-in-with-chatgpt-interest/).\n- OpenAI redirects only to `127.0.0.1`. Something must answer on that address. Vite listens on `::1` by default. The `ts-react-chat` example runs a small script on `127.0.0.1:3000` that redirects to `localhost:3000`.\n- Keep the app on `localhost`, because passkey storage does not work on an IP address. The callback lands on `127.0.0.1`, then `completeChatGptSignIn` sends the browser back to `localhost`.\n- The callback page must be at `/auth/callback`.\n\n### 1. Add the sign-in button\n\nCall `startChatGptSignIn` from a click. `agentName` is your app name. OpenAI shows it on the consent screen.\n\n```tsx\nimport { startChatGptSignIn } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai/siwc\";\n\nexport function ChatGptButton() {\n  return (\n    <button\n      type=\"button\"\n      onClick={() => {\n        void startChatGptSignIn({ agentName: \"My App\" });\n      }}\n    >\n      Continue with ChatGPT\n    </button>\n  );\n}\n```\n\n### 2. Finish on `/auth/callback`\n\nRender this component on the `/auth/callback` route. It exchanges the code when the page loads. Then the user clicks to save.\n\n```tsx\nimport { useEffect, useRef, useState } from \"react\";\nimport {\n  completeChatGptSignIn,\n  saveChatGptSignIn,\n} from \"@tanstack/ai-openai/siwc\";\nimport type { ChatGptSignIn } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai/siwc\";\nimport { byok } from \"./byok\";\n\nexport function ChatGptCallback() {\n  const started = useRef(false);\n  const [signIn, setSignIn] = useState<ChatGptSignIn | null>(null);\n  const [error, setError] = useState(\"\");\n\n  useEffect(() => {\n    // The code works one time. Strict Mode runs effects two times.\n    if (started.current) return;\n    started.current = true;\n    completeChatGptSignIn().then(setSignIn, (caught: unknown) => {\n      setError(caught instanceof Error ? caught.message : \"Sign-in failed\");\n    });\n  }, []);\n\n  if (error) return <p>{error}</p>;\n  if (!signIn) return <p>Finishing sign-in...</p>;\n  return (\n    <button\n      type=\"button\"\n      onClick={() => {\n        void saveChatGptSignIn(byok, signIn);\n      }}\n    >\n      Save ChatGPT sign-in\n    </button>\n  );\n}\n```\n\nThe save needs a click because passkey storage shows a browser prompt. The refresh token goes into a second keyring slot. No send attaches that slot, so the refresh token stays in the browser.\n\n### 3. Refresh the token\n\nThe access token lasts one hour. Call `refreshChatGptSignIn` on a timer:\n\n```tsx\nimport { useEffect } from \"react\";\nimport { refreshChatGptSignIn } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai/siwc\";\nimport { byok } from \"./byok\";\n\nexport function useChatGptRefresh() {\n  useEffect(() => {\n    const refresh = () => {\n      refreshChatGptSignIn(byok).catch(console.error);\n    };\n    refresh();\n    const timer = setInterval(refresh, 60_000);\n    return () => clearInterval(timer);\n  }, []);\n}\n```\n\nThe call does nothing until the token has less than five minutes left. If OpenAI rejects the refresh token, the call clears the sign-in. Then the user must sign in again.\n\n### 4. Read the token on the relay\n\nThe relay code is the same as for a pasted key. Add `store: false`, because the ChatGPT route requires it.\n\n```typescript\nimport {\n  chat,\n  chatParamsFromRequest,\n  toServerSentEventsResponse,\n} from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { createOpenaiChat } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\nimport { openaiByok } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai/byok\";\nimport { byokMissing, getByokKey } from \"@tanstack/ai/byok/server\";\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const params = await chatParamsFromRequest(request);\n  const apiKey = getByokKey(request, openaiByok);\n  if (!apiKey) return byokMissing(openaiByok);\n\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: createOpenaiChat(\"gpt-6-astra\", apiKey),\n    messages: params.messages,\n    threadId: params.threadId,\n    runId: params.runId,\n    modelOptions: { store: false },\n  });\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream);\n}\n```\n\n`store: false` also works with an API key. A ChatGPT token does not start with `sk-`, so use that test if you must send different options.\n\nThe ChatGPT route has these limits:\n\n- Use a model that the user's ChatGPT plan includes.\n- Do not send `temperature`, `top_p`, `max_output_tokens`, `metadata`, or `previous_response_id`.\n- Hosted tools do not work. This includes image generation, file search, code interpreter, computer use, and hosted MCP.\n- Audio input and transcription do not work.\n\nClick **Continue with ChatGPT**, approve, save, then send a message. The relay calls OpenAI on the user's ChatGPT plan.\n\nThe `ts-react-chat` example has this flow in its key dialog.\n\n## Configuration\n\n```typescript\nimport { createOpenaiChat, type OpenAITextConfig } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\n\nconst config: Omit<OpenAITextConfig, \"apiKey\"> = {\n  organization: \"org-...\", // Optional\n  baseURL: \"https://api.openai.com/v1\", // Optional, for custom endpoints\n};\n\nconst adapter = createOpenaiChat(\"gpt-5.2\", process.env.OPENAI_API_KEY!, config);\n```\n\n### Tools that cannot use strict mode\n\nOpenAI holds tool arguments to the schema only when the tool is sent with `strict: true`. Some schemas cannot be strict, for example a schema that uses `$ref`, `z.any()`, or `z.record()`. The adapter sends these tools with `strict: false`, so the tool still works. The model can then return arguments that do not match the schema.\n\nIn development, the adapter logs a warning once for each of these tools:\n\n```txt\ntool \"lookup_user\" sent with strict: false: schema uses $ref, which strict mode does not support\n```\n\nTo get strict mode back, change the schema so that the reason goes away. If you accept a non-strict tool, turn the warning off in the adapter config:\n\n```typescript\nimport { createOpenaiChat } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\n\nconst adapter = createOpenaiChat(\"gpt-6-astra\", process.env.OPENAI_API_KEY!, {\n  strictFallbackWarning: false,\n});\n```\n\nThe warning never runs when `NODE_ENV` is `production`. The same option works on every adapter built on the OpenAI API, for example Groq, Bedrock, and Vercel AI Gateway.\n \n## Example: Chat Completion\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat, toServerSentEventsResponse } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiText } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const { messages } = await request.json();\n\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: openaiText(\"gpt-5.2\"),\n    messages,\n  });\n\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream);\n}\n```\n\n## Example: With Tools\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat, toServerSentEventsResponse, toolDefinition } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiText } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\nimport { z } from \"zod\";\n\nconst getWeatherDef = toolDefinition({\n  name: \"get_weather\",\n  description: \"Get the current weather\",\n  inputSchema: z.object({\n    location: z.string(),\n  }),\n});\n\nconst getWeather = getWeatherDef.server(async ({ location }) => {\n  // Fetch weather data\n  return { temperature: 72, conditions: \"sunny\" };\n});\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const { messages } = await request.json();\n\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: openaiText(\"gpt-5.2\"),\n    messages,\n    tools: [getWeather],\n  });\n\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream);\n}\n```\n\n## Model Options\n\nOpenAI supports various provider-specific options. Sampling parameters live here too — `temperature`, `top_p`, and `max_output_tokens` (the Responses API token-limit key) — rather than as root-level props on `chat()`:\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiText } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: openaiText(\"gpt-5.2\"),\n  messages: [{ role: \"user\", content: \"Hello!\" }],\n  modelOptions: {\n    temperature: 0.7,\n    max_output_tokens: 1000,\n    top_p: 0.9,\n  },\n});\n```\n\n> The `openaiChatCompletions` adapter targets `/v1/chat/completions`, where the token-limit key is `max_tokens` (not `max_output_tokens`). If you previously passed `temperature` / `topP` / `maxTokens` at the root of `chat()`, see [Moving Sampling Options into modelOptions](../migration/sampling-options-to-model-options).\n\n### Reasoning\n\nEnable reasoning for models that support it (e.g., GPT-5, O3). This allows the model to show its reasoning process, which is streamed as `thinking` chunks:\n\n```typescript ignore\nmodelOptions: {\n  reasoning: {\n    effort: \"medium\", // \"none\" | \"minimal\" | \"low\" | \"medium\" | \"high\"\n    summary: \"detailed\", // \"auto\" | \"detailed\" (optional)\n  },\n}\n```\n\nWhen reasoning is enabled, the model's reasoning process is streamed separately from the response text and appears as a collapsible thinking section in the UI.\n\n## Summarization\n\nSummarize long text content:\n\n```typescript\nimport { summarize } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiSummarize } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\n\nconst result = await summarize({\n  adapter: openaiSummarize(\"gpt-5-mini\"),\n  text: \"Your long text to summarize...\",\n  maxLength: 100,\n  style: \"concise\", // \"concise\" | \"bullet-points\" | \"paragraph\"\n});\n\nconsole.log(result.summary);\n```\n\n## Embeddings\n\nGenerate embedding vectors with the text-embedding-3 models:\n\n```typescript\nimport { embed } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiEmbedding } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\n\nconst result = await embed({\n  adapter: openaiEmbedding(\"text-embedding-3-small\"),\n  input: [\"a red guitar\", \"a blue drum kit\"],\n});\n\nconsole.log(result.embeddings[0]?.vector);\nconsole.log(result.usage?.promptTokens);\n```\n\nBoth models support Matryoshka dimension reduction via the top-level `dimensions` option:\n\n```typescript\nimport { embed } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiEmbedding } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\n\nconst result = await embed({\n  adapter: openaiEmbedding(\"text-embedding-3-large\"),\n  input: \"a red guitar\",\n  dimensions: 1024,\n});\n```\n\nSee the [Embeddings guide](../embeddings.md) for the full API.\n\n## Image Generation\n\nGenerate images:\n\n```typescript\nimport { generateImage } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiImage } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\n\nconst result = await generateImage({\n  adapter: openaiImage(\"gpt-image-2\"),\n  prompt: \"A futuristic cityscape at sunset\",\n  numberOfImages: 1,\n  size: \"1024x1024\",\n});\n\nconsole.log(result.images);\n```\n\n### Image Model Options\n\n```typescript\nimport { generateImage } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiImage } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\n\nconst result = await generateImage({\n  adapter: openaiImage(\"gpt-image-2\"),\n  prompt: \"...\",\n  modelOptions: {\n    quality: \"high\", // \"high\" | \"medium\" | \"low\" | \"auto\"\n  },\n});\n```\n\n## Text-to-Speech\n\nGenerate speech from text:\n\n```typescript\nimport { generateSpeech } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiSpeech } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\n\nconst result = await generateSpeech({\n  adapter: openaiSpeech(\"tts-1\"),\n  text: \"Hello, welcome to TanStack AI!\",\n  voice: \"alloy\",\n  format: \"mp3\",\n});\n\n// result.audio contains base64-encoded audio\nconsole.log(result.format); // \"mp3\"\n```\n\n### TTS Voices\n\nAvailable voices: `alloy`, `echo`, `fable`, `onyx`, `nova`, `shimmer`, `ash`, `ballad`, `coral`, `sage`, `verse`\n\n### TTS Model Options\n\n```typescript\nimport { generateSpeech } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiSpeech } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\n\nconst result = await generateSpeech({\n  adapter: openaiSpeech(\"tts-1-hd\"),\n  text: \"High quality speech\",\n  modelOptions: {\n    instructions: \"Speak slowly and clearly.\", // voice instructions (not supported by tts-1/tts-1-hd)\n  },\n});\n```\n\n## Transcription\n\nTranscribe audio to text:\n\n```typescript\nimport { generateTranscription } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiTranscription } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\nimport { audioFile } from \"./audio\";\n\nconst result = await generateTranscription({\n  adapter: openaiTranscription(\"whisper-1\"),\n  audio: audioFile, // File object or base64 string\n  language: \"en\",\n});\n\nconsole.log(result.text); // Transcribed text\n```\n\n### Transcription Model Options\n\n```typescript\nimport { generateTranscription } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiTranscription } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\nimport { audioFile } from \"./audio\";\n\nconst result = await generateTranscription({\n  adapter: openaiTranscription(\"whisper-1\"),\n  audio: audioFile,\n  responseFormat: \"verbose_json\",\n  prompt: \"Technical terms: API, SDK\",\n  modelOptions: {\n    temperature: 0,\n    timestamp_granularities: [\"word\", \"segment\"],\n  },\n});\n\n// Access the transcribed text\nconsole.log(result.text);\n```\n\n### Speaker Diarization\n\nUse `gpt-4o-transcribe-diarize` for speaker-labeled transcripts:\n\n```typescript\nimport { generateTranscription } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiTranscription } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\nimport { meetingAudioFile } from \"./audio\";\n\nconst result = await generateTranscription({\n  adapter: openaiTranscription(\"gpt-4o-transcribe-diarize\"),\n  audio: meetingAudioFile,\n  modelOptions: {\n    known_speaker_names: [\"agent\", \"customer\"],\n    known_speaker_references: [\n      \"data:audio/wav;base64,...\",\n      \"data:audio/wav;base64,...\",\n    ],\n  },\n});\n\nfor (const segment of result.segments ?? []) {\n  console.log(segment.speaker, segment.start, segment.end, segment.text);\n}\n```\n\nWhen no response format is specified, `gpt-4o-transcribe-diarize` requests default to `response_format: \"diarized_json\"` and `chunking_strategy: \"auto\"`; passing a top-level `responseFormat` of `\"json\"` or `\"text\"` opts out of speaker segments. `known_speaker_names` and `known_speaker_references` must be provided together (up to 4, matching lengths). OpenAI does not support `prompt`, `include`, or `timestamp_granularities` with diarized transcription.\n\n## Evaluate\n\nSometimes you need an answer that your code can branch on, not chat text. Examples are a queue name, an urgency level, or a yes or no.\nUse `openaiDecider` with `decide()` to ask typed questions about one shared `state`. The adapter calls the OpenAI Decisions API (`/v1/decisions`):\n\n```typescript\nimport { decide, choice, score, boolean } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiDecider } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\n\nconst ticket = {\n  subject: \"Charged twice for the same invoice\",\n  body: \"Please refund the extra payment.\",\n};\n\nconst result = await decide({\n  adapter: openaiDecider(\"gpt-6-luna\"),\n  state: ticket,\n  questions: {\n    queue: choice({\n      instructions: \"Which team should handle this ticket?\",\n      options: {\n        billing: \"Payments, invoices, refunds\",\n        tech: \"Bugs, outages, integrations\",\n        sales: \"Pricing, upgrades, new accounts\",\n      },\n    }),\n    urgency: score({\n      instructions: \"How urgent is this ticket?\",\n      levels: [\"low\", \"medium\", \"high\"],\n    }),\n    refund: boolean({\n      instructions: \"Is the customer asking for a refund?\",\n    }),\n  },\n});\n\nconsole.log(result.queue.value); // \"billing\"\nconsole.log(result.urgency.value); // \"medium\"\nconsole.log(result.refund.value); // true\nconsole.log(result.meta.usage);\n```\n\n`openaiDecider` reads `OPENAI_API_KEY` from the environment. To pass a key yourself, use `createOpenaiDecider(\"gpt-6-luna\", \"sk-...\")`.\n\nGood to know:\n\n- `gpt-6-luna` is the only Decisions model.\n- An object `state` goes to OpenAI as JSON text.\n- If OpenAI refuses to answer a question, `decide()` throws an error with the name of that question.\n- `boolean()` criteria work. The adapter adds the true and false meanings to the instructions.\n\nSee the [Evaluate guide](../evaluate/evaluate) for question helpers, the result shape, abort, and middleware.\n\n## Environment Variables\n\nSet your API key in environment variables:\n\n```bash\nOPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...\n```\n\n## API Reference\n\nEvery factory pair follows the same shape: the short factory (`openaiText`, `openaiImage`, …) reads `OPENAI_API_KEY` from the environment, while the `create*` variant takes an explicit API key. Both take `model` as the first argument.\n\n### `openaiText(model, config?)`\n\nCreates an OpenAI text adapter against the Responses API (`/v1/responses`) using `OPENAI_API_KEY` from the environment.\n\n**Parameters:**\n\n- `model` - OpenAI chat model id (e.g. `\"gpt-5.2\"`, `\"gpt-4o-mini\"`)\n- `config?.organization` - Organization ID (optional)\n- `config?.baseURL` - Custom base URL (optional)\n\n### `createOpenaiChat(model, apiKey, config?)`\n\nCreates an OpenAI text adapter (Responses API) with an explicit API key.\n\n### `openaiChatCompletions(model, config?)`\n\nCreates an OpenAI text adapter that targets `/v1/chat/completions` instead of the Responses API. See [Chat Completions API](#chat-completions-api) for when to use this over `openaiText`.\n\n### `createOpenaiChatCompletions(model, apiKey, config?)`\n\nCreates an OpenAI chat-completions adapter with an explicit API key.\n\n### `openaiSummarize(model, config?)` / `createOpenaiSummarize(model, apiKey, config?)`\n\nCreates an OpenAI summarization adapter.\n\n### `openaiImage(model, config?)` / `createOpenaiImage(model, apiKey, config?)`\n\nCreates an OpenAI image generation adapter (DALL-E, gpt-image).\n\n### `openaiSpeech(model, config?)` / `createOpenaiSpeech(model, apiKey, config?)`\n\nCreates an OpenAI text-to-speech adapter.\n\n### `openaiTranscription(model, config?)` / `createOpenaiTranscription(model, apiKey, config?)`\n\nCreates an OpenAI transcription adapter for Whisper, GPT-4o transcription, and GPT-4o diarized transcription models.\n\n### `openaiVideo(model, config?)` / `createOpenaiVideo(model, apiKey, config?)`\n\nCreates an OpenAI video generation adapter (Sora). _Experimental._\n\n### `openaiDecider(model, config?)` / `createOpenaiDecider(model, apiKey, config?)`\n\nCreates an OpenAI evaluate adapter for `decide()`. See [Evaluate](#evaluate) for usage.\n\n### `openaiRealtime(...)` / `openaiRealtimeToken(...)`\n\nRealtime voice adapters. See [Realtime Voice Chat](../media/realtime-chat) for usage.\n\n## Next Steps\n\n- [Getting Started](../getting-started/quick-start) - Learn the basics\n- [Tools Guide](../tools/tools) - Learn about tools\n- [Other Adapters](./anthropic) - Explore other providers\n\n## Provider Tools\n\nOpenAI exposes several native tools beyond user-defined function calls.\nImport them from `@tanstack/ai-openai/tools` and pass them into\n`chat({ tools: [...] })`.\n\n> For the full concept, a comparison matrix, and type-gating details, see\n> [Provider Tools](../tools/provider-tools.md).\n\n### `webSearchTool`\n\nEnables the model to run a web search and return grounded results with\ncitations. Pass a `WebSearchToolConfig` object (typed from the OpenAI SDK)\nto configure the tool.\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiText } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\nimport { webSearchTool } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai/tools\";\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: openaiText(\"gpt-5.2\"),\n  messages: [{ role: \"user\", content: \"What's new in AI this week?\" }],\n  tools: [webSearchTool({ type: \"web_search\" })],\n});\n```\n\n**Supported models:** GPT-4o, GPT-5, and Responses API-capable models. See [Provider Tools](../tools/provider-tools.md#which-models-support-which-tools).\n\n### `webSearchPreviewTool`\n\nThe preview variant of web search with additional options for controlling\nsearch context size and user location. Use this when you want fine-grained\ncontrol over the search context sent to the model.\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiText } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\nimport { webSearchPreviewTool } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai/tools\";\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: openaiText(\"gpt-5.2\"),\n  messages: [{ role: \"user\", content: \"Latest news about TypeScript\" }],\n  tools: [\n    webSearchPreviewTool({\n      type: \"web_search_preview_2025_03_11\",\n      search_context_size: \"high\",\n    }),\n  ],\n});\n```\n\n**Supported models:** GPT-4o and above. See [Provider Tools](../tools/provider-tools.md#which-models-support-which-tools).\n\nWhen the model uses hosted web search, the assistant tool-call part includes\n`metadata.providerExecuted: true` and the normalized `metadata.sources` array.\nOpenAI's raw search call and URL citations stay under `metadata.openai`. The\nagent loop does not execute this call in your application, and the adapter\nreplays the raw response items on the next turn.\n\n### `fileSearchTool`\n\nSearches OpenAI vector stores that you have pre-populated, letting the model\nretrieve relevant document chunks. Provide the `vector_store_ids` to search\nand optionally limit results with `max_num_results` (1–50).\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiText } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\nimport { fileSearchTool } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai/tools\";\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: openaiText(\"gpt-5.2\"),\n  messages: [{ role: \"user\", content: \"What does the handbook say about PTO?\" }],\n  tools: [\n    fileSearchTool({\n      type: \"file_search\",\n      vector_store_ids: [\"vs_abc123\"],\n      max_num_results: 5,\n    }),\n  ],\n});\n```\n\n**Supported models:** GPT-4o and above. See [Provider Tools](../tools/provider-tools.md#which-models-support-which-tools).\n\n### `imageGenerationTool`\n\nAllows the model to generate images inline during a conversation using\nDALL-E/GPT-Image. Pass quality, size, and style options via the config object.\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiText } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\nimport { imageGenerationTool } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai/tools\";\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: openaiText(\"gpt-5.2\"),\n  messages: [{ role: \"user\", content: \"Draw a logo for my app\" }],\n  tools: [\n    imageGenerationTool({\n      quality: \"high\",\n      size: \"1024x1024\",\n    }),\n  ],\n});\n```\n\n**Supported models:** GPT-5 and GPT-Image-capable models. See [Provider Tools](../tools/provider-tools.md#which-models-support-which-tools).\n\n### `codeInterpreterTool`\n\nGives the model a sandboxed Python execution environment. The `container`\nfield configures the execution environment; pass the full\n`CodeInterpreterToolConfig` object.\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiText } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\nimport { codeInterpreterTool } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai/tools\";\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: openaiText(\"gpt-5.2\"),\n  messages: [{ role: \"user\", content: \"Analyse this CSV and plot a chart\" }],\n  tools: [\n    codeInterpreterTool({ type: \"code_interpreter\", container: { type: \"auto\" } }),\n  ],\n});\n```\n\n**Supported models:** GPT-4o and above. See [Provider Tools](../tools/provider-tools.md#which-models-support-which-tools).\n\n### `mcpTool`\n\nConnects the model to a remote MCP (Model Context Protocol) server, exposing\nall its capabilities as callable tools. Provide either `server_url` or\n`connector_id` — not both.\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiText } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\nimport { mcpTool } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai/tools\";\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: openaiText(\"gpt-5.2\"),\n  messages: [{ role: \"user\", content: \"List my GitHub issues\" }],\n  tools: [\n    mcpTool({\n      server_url: \"https://mcp.example.com\",\n      server_label: \"github\",\n    }),\n  ],\n});\n```\n\n**Supported models:** GPT-4o and above. See [Provider Tools](../tools/provider-tools.md#which-models-support-which-tools).\n\n### `computerUseTool`\n\nLets the model observe a virtual desktop via screenshots and interact with\nit using keyboard and mouse events. Provide the display dimensions and the\nexecution environment type.\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiText } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\nimport { computerUseTool } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai/tools\";\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: openaiText(\"computer-use-preview\"),\n  messages: [{ role: \"user\", content: \"Open Chrome and navigate to example.com\" }],\n  tools: [\n    computerUseTool({\n      type: \"computer_use_preview\",\n      display_width: 1024,\n      display_height: 768,\n      environment: \"browser\",\n    }),\n  ],\n});\n```\n\n**Supported models:** `computer-use-preview`. See [Provider Tools](../tools/provider-tools.md#which-models-support-which-tools).\n\n### `localShellTool`\n\nThe model returns a `local_shell` tool call. Your app runs the command. Then your app sends the output back on the next request. `localShellTool()` takes no arguments. Add it to `tools`.\n\nMatch `toolName` on `TOOL_CALL_START`. Read `input` on the `TOOL_CALL_END` with the same `toolCallId`. `input.command` is the command. `input.env` is the environment variables.\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiText } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\nimport { localShellTool } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai/tools\";\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: openaiText(\"gpt-5.6\"),\n  messages: [{ role: \"user\", content: \"Run the test suite and summarise failures\" }],\n  tools: [localShellTool()],\n});\n\nlet localShellCallId: string | undefined;\nfor await (const chunk of stream) {\n  if (chunk.type === \"TOOL_CALL_START\" && chunk.toolName === \"local_shell\") {\n    localShellCallId = chunk.toolCallId;\n  }\n  if (chunk.type === \"TOOL_CALL_END\" && chunk.toolCallId === localShellCallId) {\n    console.log(chunk.input);\n  }\n}\n```\n\nSend the command output as the tool result. Use `{ output: string }`, or a string. The next request sends `local_shell_call_output`.\n\n**Supported models:** GPT-5.x and other agent-capable models. See [Provider Tools](../tools/provider-tools.md#which-models-support-which-tools).\n\n### `shellTool`\n\n`shellTool()` gives the model a shell. A container environment runs on OpenAI. A local environment runs in your app.\n\nWhen your app must run the commands, pass `environment: { type: \"local\" }`. Match `toolName` on `TOOL_CALL_START`. Read `input` on the `TOOL_CALL_END` with the same `toolCallId`. `input.commands` is the command list. `input.timeout_ms` is the time limit. `input.max_output_length` is the output limit.\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiText } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\nimport { shellTool } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai/tools\";\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: openaiText(\"gpt-5.6\"),\n  messages: [{ role: \"user\", content: \"Count lines in all JS files\" }],\n  tools: [shellTool({ environment: { type: \"local\" } })],\n});\n\nlet shellCallId: string | undefined;\nfor await (const chunk of stream) {\n  if (chunk.type === \"TOOL_CALL_START\" && chunk.toolName === \"shell\") {\n    shellCallId = chunk.toolCallId;\n  }\n  if (chunk.type === \"TOOL_CALL_END\" && chunk.toolCallId === shellCallId) {\n    console.log(chunk.input);\n  }\n}\n```\n\nReturn one result per command:\n\n```typescript\nconst shellResult = {\n  output: [\n    {\n      stdout: \"12\\n\",\n      stderr: \"\",\n      outcome: { type: \"exit\" as const, exit_code: 0 },\n    },\n  ],\n};\n```\n\n`outcome.type` is `\"exit\"` or `\"timeout\"`. The next request sends `shell_call_output`. If the same response has no `shell_call_output`, a shell call with no environment comes back to your app.\n\nA container environment does not come back as a tool call. Pass `environment` to attach that container and hosted skills.\n\n**Supported models:** GPT-5.x and other agent-capable models. Responses API\nonly — Chat Completions does not support the shell tool. See [Provider Tools](../tools/provider-tools.md#which-models-support-which-tools).\n\n#### Attaching hosted skills\n\nPass `environment.skills` to load provider-managed skill bundles into the\nshell's container (Responses API only).\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat, toServerSentEventsResponse } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiText } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\nimport { shellTool } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai/tools\";\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const { messages } = await request.json();\n\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: openaiText(\"gpt-5.2\"),\n    messages,\n    tools: [\n      shellTool({\n        environment: {\n          type: \"container_auto\",\n          skills: [\n            { type: \"skill_reference\", skill_id: \"skill_abc\", version: \"2\" },\n          ],\n        },\n      }),\n    ],\n  });\n\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream);\n}\n```\n\nFor the full reference — skill shape, `version` string format, and the\nAnthropic equivalent — see [Provider Skills](../tools/provider-skills.md).\n\n### `applyPatchTool`\n\nThe model returns an `apply_patch` tool call. Your app applies the diff. Then your app sends the result back. `applyPatchTool()` takes no arguments. Add it to `tools`.\n\nMatch `toolName` on `TOOL_CALL_START`. Read `input` on the `TOOL_CALL_END` with the same `toolCallId`. `input.operation` is one file change. `operation.type` is `create_file`, `update_file`, or `delete_file`. `operation.path` is the file path. `create_file` and `update_file` also include `operation.diff`.\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiText } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\nimport { applyPatchTool } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai/tools\";\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: openaiText(\"gpt-5.6\"),\n  messages: [{ role: \"user\", content: \"Fix the import paths in src/index.ts\" }],\n  tools: [applyPatchTool()],\n});\n\nlet patchCallId: string | undefined;\nfor await (const chunk of stream) {\n  if (chunk.type === \"TOOL_CALL_START\" && chunk.toolName === \"apply_patch\") {\n    patchCallId = chunk.toolCallId;\n  }\n  if (chunk.type === \"TOOL_CALL_END\" && chunk.toolCallId === patchCallId) {\n    console.log(chunk.input);\n  }\n}\n```\n\nSend this object as the tool result. The next request sends `apply_patch_call_output`.\n\n```typescript\nconst patchResult = {\n  status: \"completed\" as const,\n  output: \"Updated src/index.ts\",\n};\n```\n\nIf the patch fails, set `status` to `\"failed\"`. Put the error text in `output`. Keep `applyPatchTool()` in `tools` on the next request. A patch-only turn has no text. If you use `chat({ stream: false })`, `text` is empty. Read the `apply_patch` tool call from `chunks` with the same checks as the loop above.\n\n**Supported models:** GPT-5.x and other agent-capable models. See [Provider Tools](../tools/provider-tools.md#which-models-support-which-tools).\n\n### `customTool`\n\nDefines a custom Responses API tool with an explicit name, description, and\nformat. Use this when none of the structured tool types fits your use case.\nUnlike branded provider tools, `customTool` returns a plain `Tool` and is\naccepted by any chat model.\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiText } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\nimport { customTool } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai/tools\";\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: openaiText(\"gpt-5.2\"),\n  messages: [{ role: \"user\", content: \"Look up order #1234\" }],\n  tools: [\n    customTool({\n      type: \"custom\",\n      name: \"lookup_order\",\n      description: \"Look up the status of a customer order by order ID\",\n    }),\n  ],\n});\n```\n\n**Supported models:** all Responses API models. See [Provider Tools](../tools/provider-tools.md#which-models-support-which-tools).\n"}
